{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values","id":1386571,"title":"How useful is Hardness at low values?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-07T17:58:21-07:00","id":1386571,"title":"How useful is Hardness at low values?","content":"Pretty much as the title. There are plenty of effects that give very low values of Hardness: Durability of Oak Meditation gives 4, the Twilight anima power gives 5, etc. So how often are decisive attacks launched with so little initiative behind them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T19:12:30-07:00","id":1386592,"title":"","content":"For one thing, any Hardness at all makes you immune to a Dragon-Blooded's anima flux, which is a big deal when 5 of them are going all super sentai on you. There are also a bunch of non initiative-based decisives that start at very low values like Essence + extra successes and things like that so you might be able to dodge some of those. With 5 Hardness you have a decent chance of no-selling a Death of Obsidian Butterflies.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that you can use charms to reduce the damage of the attack before comparing to Hardness, like Earth Bears Witness, which effectively &quot;extends&quot; the reach of your Hardness a couple more points, which can catch your opponent off guard.<br /> <br /> Dudes that like poison will often try to nick you with a low initiative decisive because any damage is enough to get the poison on you. I've had one White Veil assasin have a bad time with this because their organ-liquefying charms cost like 5 or 6 initiative before rolling the attack which put them just below that Hardness line.<br /> <br /> Finally, there are flurries, which Solars in particular love. If Dawn McSwordy has 20 initiative or less he won't be able to do a full Invincible Fury of the Dawn on you, he'll have to beef up his base damage or settle for fewer attacks. It's admitedly not a lot, but it does mitigate <i>some</i> damage.<br /> <br /> So in conclusion, not useless, but not likely to come up that often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T19:28:04-07:00","id":1386594,"title":"","content":"I as a Storyteller have more than once launched decisive attacks from five or fewer Initiative.<br /> <br /> Consider, after all, that success or failure won\u2019t put you at <i>significantly</i> more of a disadvantage, versus the possibility that successfully wounding the opponent may shift the dice in your favor. Especially if you and your buddies outnumber the other guy and his buddies.<br /> <br /> Plus giving them a little wound like that helps ramp up the tension and sense of danger, and makes any conflicts that take place after (but before they\u2019ve had time to heal) more difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T19:55:02-07:00","id":1386600,"title":"","content":"Also without it you can get nickel-and-dimed over the course of a fight or a long series of fights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T21:55:45-07:00","id":1386611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhanjRho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values#post1386571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much as the title. There are plenty of effects that give very low values of Hardness: Durability of Oak Meditation gives 4, the Twilight anima power gives 5, etc. So how often are decisive attacks launched with so little initiative behind them?</div> </div> </div> </div>How can that question be answered? Can we effectively survey the population of Exalted players?<br /> <br /> I feel as though this facet of game design is less about how &quot;often&quot; a thing happens and more about covering the contingency of it ever happening at all. Just to cover the variety of options and create useful countersigns for them.<br /> <br /> Somewhere out there I expect there's somebody who's run a probability simulation that proposes that low Initiative decisive attacks aren't worth the cost of launching them, and might argue that low Hardness is thus worthless. It makes me wonder how many people playing the game are all that concerned with the probabilities and optimal solutions, as opposed to just playing things how they feel useful in the moment, or even just for the variety.<br /> <br /> I also suppose that a low Initiative decisive gives recourse to somebody frustrated by an inability to get their withering attacks in often enough (or with good enough numbers to get over the soak), and that the way the dice work makes it just possible enough that those few dice could turn up something that actually shifts the tide. I wonder if even the player focused on the number crunching feels tense when four damage dice all turn up successes, and now their character is a lot closer to Incapacitation.<br /> <br /> The odds of the next four damage dice turning up such numbers might be low, but are you sure you want to risk it? The 5 Hardness doesn't cost that much, does it? Just to make killing you something that they need to earn, rather than getting from confidently chasing a fluke born of frustration.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it might lend a little something to the power fantasy to deny the person struggling to raise Initiative even the Hail Mary of attacking you with little Initiative.<br /> <br /> I'd say these possibilities are worth addressing even if they're a minority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T23:06:37-07:00","id":1386621,"title":"","content":"Hardness is like Damage resistance or Energy resistance in D&amp;D cant count the number of times people either wiped or saved by resist acid from Melfs acid arrow or other environment damaage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel","name":"Cypheriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T23:29:05-07:00","id":1386625,"title":"","content":"When you have a somewhat larger group of people (like a group of a half-dozen or more mortals) fighting one stronger individual (like maybe one of the Exalted), it's not a bad tactic for members of that group to throw out a bunch of small decisive attacks every turn to try and take the stronger opponent out of the fight quickly (or at least get a few hits on that enemy so that wound penalties start applying) rather than try and spend time trying to build up larger initiative pools. Basically each member's turn rolls around they could throw out a decisive attack, then reset to base initiative (3) and then throw out another decisive attack for 3 damage on their next turn.<br /> <br /> Having Hardness of 4 or higher completely shuts that tactic down. It makes it so that enemies <i>have</i> to spend a turn or two landing withering attacks to build their Initiative up above your Hardness level before they can even think about throwing out a decisive attack, which definitely helps when fighting against large groups of enemies.<br /> <br /> Overall I find lower Hardness to be much less useful in Exalt on Exalt fights, or fights between Exalted and significantly powerful foes, outside of specific cases like an Exalt using a Charm that allows her to make multiple decisive attacks but requires her to split her initiative pool (in such a case she would have to make sure her decisive dice pools exceed your Hardness rating since making one attack for 12 decisive damage would be more useful than making 5 attacks for 3 decisive damage if you have a Hardness of 4).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T04:25:05-07:00","id":1386657,"title":"","content":"Actually even Hardness 3 stops 3i decisive attacks. They have to exceed your hardness, not match it, to overcome it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T04:54:43-07:00","id":1386659,"title":"","content":"I've not really seen it be useful. Seems like it'd be useful against Anima Flux, but it's a bit pricey (except against the more powerful Flux effects like Fire and Earth). Also seems like it'd be useful against multi-attack spam (where you throw 5 attacks, but each one does like 2 damage dice), but that's not something either PCs or NPCs really use in the games I play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T05:31:24-07:00","id":1386662,"title":"","content":"Maybe they\u2019re not using them <i>because</i> of Hardness.<br /> <br /> Better to have it and not need it, as they say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T05:44:57-07:00","id":1386664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1386625#post1386625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you have a somewhat larger group of people (like a group of a half-dozen or more mortals) fighting one stronger individual (like maybe one of the Exalted), it's not a bad tactic for members of that group to throw out a bunch of small decisive attacks every turn to try and take the stronger opponent out of the fight quickly (or at least get a few hits on that enemy so that wound penalties start applying) rather than try and spend time trying to build up larger initiative pools. Basically each member's turn rolls around they could throw out a decisive attack, then reset to base initiative (3) and then throw out another decisive attack for 3 damage on their next turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's similar to what I do.<br /> <br /> Though less emphasis on multiple opponents and more characters who probably won't be conscious next round will try to accomplish something before they get taken out. So it's a popular choice for a mortal sidekick or the Satrap's small annoying dog etc since the PC being attacked has to prioritise between taking them remotely seriously or risking embarrassment.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T08:24:25-07:00","id":1386698,"title":"","content":"I've not seen it be useful in the combats I've run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T15:05:00-07:00","id":1386789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1386662#post1386662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe they\u2019re not using them <i>because</i> of Hardness.<br /> <br /> Better to have it and not need it, as they say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the source of the Hardness might be a bigger issue here though.<br /> <br /> Having Artifact armor, or being a Twilight that has a Hardness power as part of the package is a bit different than having to dip into the Resistance Charms.<br /> <br /> Artifacts are always on when you're wearing them, Twilight's Anima goes on for free as full, etc, where DoOM gets consistently less useful the more attackers you're dealing with.<br /> <br /> There's also the issue of Hardness effectively being Perilous unless noted otherwise (which Twilight Anima Hardness gets). When you're at your most vulnerable, most sources of Hardness aren't there to help keep you safe.<br /> <br /> So while better to have it and not need it, it's better to get it as part of a package of stuff you're probably going to be using more of the rest, than taking something that's only purpose is giving you Hardness.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T15:21:36-07:00","id":1386791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1386659#post1386659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've not really seen it be useful. Seems like it'd be useful against Anima Flux, but it's a bit pricey (except against the more powerful Flux effects like Fire and Earth). Also seems like it'd be useful against multi-attack spam (where you throw 5 attacks, but each one does like 2 damage dice), but that's not something either PCs or NPCs really use in the games I play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah mostly the same. I'd like Hardness to be underlined a bit more during my games, the same way Soak gets put forward for character who has them, but not like the way Soak scales because I'm not really interested in putting 25 damage enemies to have the possibility to threaten one player","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T15:33:25-07:00","id":1386796,"title":"","content":"So, for an NPC, there's basically no reason not to be using a Decisive on every attack. Except Hardness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T15:43:50-07:00","id":1386800,"title":"","content":"It's been plenty useful here. In no small part because it's a game on the blessed isle and there's plenty dbs.<br /> <br /> Don't forget, too, that pricing hardness is not really pricing <i>hardness</i>, it's pricing charms, armor and the like. They tend to do more than just give a smidge of hardness.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 05-08-2020, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T15:56:00-07:00","id":1386803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1386625#post1386625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you have a somewhat larger group of people (like a group of a half-dozen or more mortals) fighting one stronger individual (like maybe one of the Exalted)</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the Exalt is probably the NPC and the mortals are the player characters.<br /> <br /> A storyteller can give an NPC whatever Hardness he feels best, but the players are the ones needing to decide how much investment Hardness is worth for them.<br /> <br /> And no PC is going to fight half-a-dozen individual opponents at once, and no battle group is going to launch a decisive attack, let alone multiple decisive attacks against a single target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T16:02:42-07:00","id":1386804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1386803#post1386803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then the Exalt is probably the NPC and the mortals are the player characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does that follow?<br /> <br /> \u200bI've had games where one PC fought a bunch of NPCs by himself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1386803#post1386803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no PC is going to fight half-a-dozen individual opponents at once...</div> </div> </div> </div>To the contrary, that has happened in games of mine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1386803#post1386803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and no battle group is going to launch a decisive attack, let alone multiple decisive attacks against a single target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Battle groups generally don't make decisive attacks. (They can do gambits, but that's a little different and doesn't interact with Hardness.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T17:28:26-07:00","id":1386831,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of us wouldn't really see a 1-on-6 fight where the six shouldn't be turned into a BG as a situation were Hardness is the line between winning and losing. The risk of losing Hardness from initiative crash from all those enemies being able to attack you is one among many reasons that Hardness doesn't seem as useful as it could be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T18:00:38-07:00","id":1386841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1386831#post1386831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a lot of us wouldn't really see a 1-on-6 fight where the six shouldn't be turned into a BG as a situation were Hardness is the line between winning and losing. The risk of losing Hardness from initiative crash from all those enemies being able to attack you is one among many reasons that Hardness doesn't seem as useful as it could be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You could perhaps houserule that Hardness was the negative initiative threshold a battlegroup had to pull you down to before its attacks started doing lethal damage. So if you had Hardness 5, you'd have to be at -5 init before they started actually hurting you. If you did that, though, I'd suggest that it would be better to let them do the damage to you as soon as the attack went over your threshold - that is, if you have Hardness 5, if a battlegroup attacked and did enough to drop you to -6 initiative, you'd actually go to -5, and take two dice of lethal damage. The current system, where the battlegroup only does lethal when you <i>start</i> crashed, feels like it would be too hard to arrange under this &quot;Hardness threshold&quot; mechanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T19:37:24-07:00","id":1386877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1386831#post1386831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a lot of us wouldn't really see a 1-on-6 fight where the six shouldn't be turned into a BG as a situation were Hardness is the line between winning and losing. The risk of losing Hardness from initiative crash from all those enemies being able to attack you is one among many reasons that Hardness doesn't seem as useful as it could be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see a lot of 6-on-1 fights necessarily, but I see a reasonable number of fights with 5 bloodapes against 4 PCs where two or three of them might just activate Principle of Motion and launch a hail of decisive claw attacks at somebody.<br /> <br /> The Bloodape's goal isn't to win at all costs, it's to claw the PC's eyes out before they get to the Green Sun Prince who's enslaved this province. I mean, in universe their goal is to kill the PCs, but initiative is not an in-universe resource that the apes are aware of. Their narrative goal is to be an interesting fight to demonstrate how deep and long this corruption has lasted, and to give the PCs a fun romp of smashing apes through stone pillars before they meet somebody who can match them properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T22:09:33-07:00","id":1386908,"title":"","content":"In my experience:<br /> <br /> 1-2: Not much use at all....unless you are fighting Dragon Bloods.<br /> 3-4: Situational useful.<br /> 5+: Fairly useful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T22:58:39-07:00","id":1386924,"title":"","content":"It is a good way to avoid an embarrassing death by a thousand paper cuts or getting group hugged to death by a sworn kinship of dragon blooded with their anima flaring. If it doesn't come up that often that is because your enemies know you probably have hardness and so don't give those low damage attacks a try to begin with and creating the illusion hardness was not used when it definitely was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T01:08:56-07:00","id":1386930,"title":"","content":"OK.<br /> <br /> While the whole &quot;Hardness was used because it stopped your enemies from even trying something,&quot; is technically true, it's also a really unsatisfying way to use something that's as valued as it is in the system.<br /> <br /> If I had a 5 dot Artifact, mastered all the Evocations, but became famous for it and I mostly use it by scaring away enemies from fighting me unless they can manipulate the situation to keep my Artifact out of it, then... I'm using it but it feels pretty weak.<br /> <br /> If the primary use of Hardness is to deter, it lacks the active punch that make for the best powers in the game. People want to have Hardness to have attacks bounce off them, not to intellectually know that some attacks didn't happen because they would have bounced off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T01:49:25-07:00","id":1386934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1386803#post1386803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then the Exalt is probably the NPC and the mortals are the player characters.<br /> <br /> A storyteller can give an NPC whatever Hardness he feels best, but the players are the ones needing to decide how much investment Hardness is worth for them.<br /> <br /> And no PC is going to fight half-a-dozen individual opponents at once, and no battle group is going to launch a decisive attack, let alone multiple decisive attacks against a single target.</div> </div> </div> </div>The battlegroup rules are not there to nerf mortals. They exist to make the ST's life easier.<br /> <br /> If you look back at 1E and 2E where Extras were actually addressed with meaningful story advice, then look at the 3E battlegroup rules (along with what Storytelling advice does exist, like the Skip It sidebar), then I maintain non-Exalted foes are <i>usually</i> important enough to the narrative to <i>not</i> run them as a battlegroup.<br /> <br /> The courtier who wraps a kingdom around her finger has Presence 3. She is probably important to the narrative. If six mortals are challenging your Exalt to a fight, they are <i>probably</i> important to the narrative -- if not, why not Skip It, or treat them as trivial opponents, or handle it narratively?<br /> <br /> A battlegroup of six mortals is for when you are confronted by three Sidereals riding their Elemental mounts, their bound demon, a lesser god AND their six mortal martial artists.<br /> <br /> If you are <i>just</i> fighting six mortals, those mortals are important to the narrative <i>by default</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1386930#post1386930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had a 5 dot Artifact, mastered all the Evocations, but became famous for it and I mostly use it by scaring away enemies from fighting me unless they can manipulate the situation to keep my Artifact out of it, then... I'm using it but it feels pretty weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>No vaguely intelligent enemy is going to march into an unwinnable meat-grinder.<br /> <br /> Unless you're delving into dungeons and fighting mindless beasts, or you Session 0 that all your enemies are idiots, then this is EXACTLY what's going to happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1386877#post1386877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bloodape's goal isn't to win at all costs, it's to claw the PC's eyes out before they get to the Green Sun Prince who's enslaved this province. I mean, in universe their goal is to kill the PCs, but initiative is not an in-universe resource that the apes are aware of. <b>Their narrative goal is to be an interesting fight</b> to demonstrate how deep and long this corruption has lasted, and to give the PCs a fun romp of smashing apes through stone pillars before they meet somebody who can match them properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree. A million times agree.<br /> <br /> The Exalted can overcome any single challenge. But they run on finite resources. Being a Solar is about rationing your awesome power, wielding your unstoppable might with the barest economy. Being a Dragon-Blooded is about husbanding your strength until you need to go all out.<br /> <br /> Little tools like Hardness 4 aren't there to beat Ligier. They're there so <i>when you get to</i> Ligier, you have more of your strength intact.<br /> <br /> Now if your ST doesn't run Exalted that way, these tools aren't going to be useful to you. Just as if your ST runs games as back-to-back white room combat encounters, your Sail Charms aren't going to be useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-09-2020, 05:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T04:04:33-07:00","id":1386944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1386930#post1386930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the primary use of Hardness is to deter, it lacks the active punch that make for the best powers in the game. People want to have Hardness to have attacks bounce off them, not to intellectually know that some attacks didn't happen because they would have bounced off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speak for yourself.<br /> <br /> The catharsis that comes from controlling the shape of the game to deny opponents even the option of certain tactical avenues may not be for you, but don't presume that it is valued by nobody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-09-2020, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T05:24:57-07:00","id":1386957,"title":"","content":"Indeed; if I buy Ready In Eight Directions Stance, I can bask in my enemies being drastically less willing to try and hit me within range of my spear. The punishing aura I exude, the statement of, \u201cSwing that arm at me, and you\u2019ll lose it,\u201d that\u2019s still something, even if I don\u2019t use the Charm in every combat, or even most of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T05:55:05-07:00","id":1386963,"title":"","content":"I must say I'm rather on Heavy Arms side in the sens that I never &quot;felt&quot; Hardness was useful (even if maybe it was), and so it didn't impact me the way for example Soak, Weapon damage, etc ... did.<br /> <br /> But maybe having something that allows to go quickly over the math (If Hardness &gt; Damage then stop) is better because it reduces the time spent doing calculations during combat. Still, none of me or my players had a &quot;good memory of Hardness&quot; because it never truly shined","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T11:44:23-07:00","id":1387026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1386934#post1386934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No vaguely intelligent enemy is going to march into an unwinnable meat-grinder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately the setting isn't meant to be full of perfectly intelligent and omniscient enemies. It feels very strange for this to be the response while praising the Blood Ape example.<br /> <br /> The point is that if the player invests in being able to do X... they should get to do X, not be satisfied with everyone being too deterred that X will happen that it rarely ever does.<br /> <br /> The narrative goal of some enemies is to provide my Artifact 5 wielding badass the chance to show off so I don't feel like it was a waste investing in all that badassery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless you're delving into dungeons and fighting mindless beasts, or you Session 0 that all your enemies are idiots, then this is EXACTLY what's going to happen. </div> </div> </div>And this feels like the worst of 2e Exalted Forumite instincts. Last I checked 3e is supposed to discourage this sort of meta where it's all about setting up &quot;required&quot; mechanical builds because otherwise the ST has to make all the enemies idiots to avoid killing you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Little tools like Hardness 4 aren't there to beat Ligier. They're there so <i>when you get to</i> Ligier, you have more of your strength intact. </div> </div> </div>This makes sense for light Artifact armor, but not so much for things like Twilight Anima or Charm based Hardness. When your Hardness is there for scene or longer, OK, you're preserving resources. If you're facing a bunch of low damage decisive attacks and have to use lots of motes to shut them all down, or risk some damage from a few of them, you're just picking which of your resources to be low on when you face Ligier.<br /> <br /> And none of this is really comparing your potential to have more strength for the big boss fight to other methods. Having a base or scene long DV that's high enough low level baddies can't hit you with an onslaught negating Charm as backup could easily have you better off that trying to rely on low level Hardness. And it'll have more utility when you fight Ligier later.<br /> <br /> If I'm worried about enemies using a lot of low initiative decisive attacks, Searing Quicksilver Flight is something a Solar can start with without going Dodge Supernal, and makes trying to spam those sorts of attacks exceedingly dangerous. Why just negate a weak attack's damage when you can cause the enemy to crash themselves for even trying such an attack? An opponent that's going to try to hit me with a 3 initiative attack is a lot more dangerous if they hit, deal no damage, and reset to 3, than if they miss and crash themselves to -5.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying low level Hardness is useless, but in the grand scheme of things, it feels like people are overselling how useful it is in context of everything else going on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now if your ST doesn't run Exalted that way, these tools aren't going to be useful to you. </div> </div> </div>The problem is &quot;that way,&quot; is, &quot;having NPCs toss out low damage decisive attacks with meaningful frequency.&quot; There's nothing in the books that gives players a strong expectation that NPCs are going to toss a bunch of base initiative decisive attacks at you. The books are very clear that Sail Charms are only really useful if you're going to have something to pilot (which is it's own issue but you don't need any sort of system mastery to figure it out).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1386944#post1386944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speak for yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel perfectly comfortable for speaking for more than myself on this one, even if sure, not every single person ever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The catharsis that comes from controlling the shape of the game to deny opponents even the option of certain tactical avenues may not be for you, but don't presume that it is valued by nobody. </div> </div> </div>I've never seen anyone that wants to use Hardness this way stick to low levels of Hardness. You can pick up heavy Artifact armor for the same price. You can go the Sorcery route and start roughly on par with medium Artifact and get up to on par with heavy as your Essence goes up.<br /> <br /> But I've also never seen anything I'd describe as catharsis happen because of Hardness. Yes, people might get that when their tactical decision making pays off, but only if they experience it doing so.<br /> <br /> The issue with Hardness, esp. low Hardness as the topic of the thread, is that it's very hard to ensure the player feels the experience of it paying off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1386957#post1386957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed; if I buy Ready In Eight Directions Stance, I can bask in my enemies being drastically less willing to try and hit me within range of my spear. The punishing aura I exude, the statement of, \u201cSwing that arm at me, and you\u2019ll lose it,\u201d that\u2019s still something, even if I don\u2019t use the Charm in every combat, or even most of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this comparison, is that you had to show off your Melee skills well enough to have gathered enough initiative to actually make Ready In Eight Directions Stance intimidating.<br /> <br /> Having the Charm alone doesn't mean much. Sitting at initiative 4 isn't such a big threat that enemies are going to be scared of attacking you. You need to get your potential decisive damage up there so your counter attacks are actually scary.<br /> <br /> There's no equivalent process with Hardness where you're going to show off how tough you are a bunch, and then everyone's too demoralized from your toughness to actually force you to break out some bigger Hardness effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 05-09-2020, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T13:39:53-07:00","id":1387065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387026#post1387026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The narrative goal of some enemies is to provide my Artifact 5 wielding badass the chance to show off so I don't feel like it was a waste investing in all that badassery.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you intentionally built and played your character to have an Artifact 5 absolutely legendary bulwark that's given you a reputation of being unkillable then that's kind of on you, isn't it? I mean if the Unconquered Sun comes down to Creation, levels the Godspear of All-Searing Noon on me and says &quot;Come, I offer a challenge, defeat me in single combat and you shall have the Throne of Heaven.&quot; I'm not ever going to take him up on that one.<br /> <br /> If I have Hardness 5 that means an enemy with 5i isn't going to attack me with their decisive, they're going to pick somebody else or they're going to wither me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387026#post1387026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this feels like the worst of 2e Exalted Forumite instincts. Last I checked 3e is supposed to discourage this sort of meta where it's all about setting up &quot;required&quot; mechanical builds because otherwise the ST has to make all the enemies idiots to avoid killing you.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kind of the opposite of that though right? In 2e if you didn't have the proper perfect suite a lot of enemies could just one-shot you. In 3e if you don't have the perfect mechanical build...then you're fine, and if you do have one that makes you really tough then enemies who aren't likewise tough, but who know that you are, are probably not going to bother without a good reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387026#post1387026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes sense for light Artifact armor, but not so much for things like Twilight Anima or Charm based Hardness. When your Hardness is there for scene or longer, OK, you're preserving resources. If you're facing a bunch of low damage decisive attacks and have to use lots of motes to shut them all down, or risk some damage from a few of them, you're just picking which of your resources to be low on when you face Ligier.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as resources go, motes are less important than health levels. You don't die when you run out of motes, you don't take a -4 penalty to all actions when you're almost out of motes. If you have to go into battle with one mote left, or one health level left, you know which one you're taking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387026#post1387026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And none of this is really comparing your potential to have more strength for the big boss fight to other methods. Having a base or scene long DV that's high enough low level baddies can't hit you with an onslaught negating Charm as backup could easily have you better off that trying to rely on low level Hardness. And it'll have more utility when you fight Ligier later.<br /> <br /> If I'm worried about enemies using a lot of low initiative decisive attacks, Searing Quicksilver Flight is something a Solar can start with without going Dodge Supernal, and makes trying to spam those sorts of attacks exceedingly dangerous. Why just negate a weak attack's damage when you can cause the enemy to crash themselves for even trying such an attack? An opponent that's going to try to hit me with a 3 initiative attack is a lot more dangerous if they hit, deal no damage, and reset to 3, than if they miss and crash themselves to -5.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Fivefold Bulwark Stance is good! It's also Essence 2, costs you your turn to set up, and costs willpower. Sometimes that's absolutely a good choice to make, but not always. Sometimes you're going to want to start the fight off yourself by doing just something else. Defend Other, flurry a weapon draw with a rise from prone, withering attack somebody, decisive attack them with charm boosted damage.<br /> <br /> 2) Searing Quicksilver Flight is also good! But it requires Dodge, and if you're a heavy armor user with a medium weapon Dodge is not your friend. Also it requires you to dodge the attack, which you can't actually ensure without a bunch of motes being spent.<br /> <br /> 3) Yes, low-level hardness is not universally insanely useful. It's not supposed to be, that's why Durability of Oak Meditation is Essence 1, Resistance 2, no pre-requisite charms, and has the 4 hardness as only one of its two effects, which also lasts for the duration of a whole tick meaning it applies to all attacks delivered on that initiative number, including flurries.<br /> <br /> 4) Durability of Oak doesn't just give you 4 hardness, it lowers Withering and Decisive damage by 2, which means the range that it shuts down attacks is actually up to 6i in addition to any other decisive lowering effects, <i>and </i>at Essence 2 it comboes with Diamond Body Prana, to get up to 9i range.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387026#post1387026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is &quot;that way,&quot; is, &quot;having NPCs toss out low damage decisive attacks with meaningful frequency.&quot; There's nothing in the books that gives players a strong expectation that NPCs are going to toss a bunch of base initiative decisive attacks at you. The books are very clear that Sail Charms are only really useful if you're going to have something to pilot (which is it's own issue but you don't need any sort of system mastery to figure it out).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very big problem with Exalted not having a DMG. It plagued my first campaigns relentlessly and really sucks. It sucks for Storytellers who feel like there's no tension, not even the illusion of tension, in any of their games, and it sucks for the guy who bought healing or Hardness charms with the idea that they might actually be useful at some point in the story.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the game kind of straight-up doesn't work if you don't play it like that. Even DnD has this problem, and even at low levels. DnD actually has a DMg though that says &quot;You should have 6-8 medium to hard encounters in a single day to make things feel right.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387026#post1387026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never seen anyone that wants to use Hardness this way stick to low levels of Hardness. You can pick up heavy Artifact armor for the same price. You can go the Sorcery route and start roughly on par with medium Artifact and get up to on par with heavy as your Essence goes up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Invulnerable Skin of Bronze is a problem spell, in my opinion. Especially with its control bonus its just too good when Solars can get sorcery with so little investment. Heavy Artifact armor is more balanced in that you can't wear it everywhere without ousting yourself as Anathema, it has a killer mobility penalty, and costs not only merit dots but also a committed 6m. Plus it's equipment that you can be separated from, whereas your charms are not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387026#post1387026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I've also never seen anything I'd describe as catharsis happen because of Hardness. Yes, people might get that when their tactical decision making pays off, but only if they experience it doing so.<br /> <br /> The issue with Hardness, esp. low Hardness as the topic of the thread, is that it's very hard to ensure the player feels the experience of it paying off.</div> </div> </div> </div>For armor hardness I can see that, but the reflexive hardness not so much. &quot;Okay James, the 6i bloodape is going to flurry a pair of decisive attacks into you. You activate Durability of Oak? Okay they glance harmlessly off your iron-hard skin, no need to roll.&quot;<br /> <br /> Unless the ST just thinks to themself &quot;Jame's character has Durability of Oak, which means that if this 6i bloodape attacks her, James can just activate that charm reflexively and negate it, which means I won't do that.&quot; which is probably too much tactical thinking on the ST's part, and maybe doesn't jive that well with the setting even. Unless this bloodape has some intel on the character that they can make their body like diamond, so if you're going to hit you'd better hit hard.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387026#post1387026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no equivalent process with Hardness where you're going to show off how tough you are a bunch, and then everyone's to demoralized form your toughness to actually force you to break out some bigger Hardness effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is exactly an equivalent to this, because Hardness Master isn't really a viable option in the game. You're not going to block a bunch of attacks with Hardness, then convert enemy withering damage to Decisive so that you can absorb it with your Hardness, then roll your Hardness and heal a number of health levels equal to the result.<br /> <br /> What will happen instead is they smash you with a withering attack, and deal no damage so they get 1i. Then hammer you with another one, and deal no damage and get only 1i. Then they say &quot;Okay, okay, fuck you, I'm not dying here without at least taking one of your god damned ears.&quot; so they throw their 9i decisive at you...and you bump your Hardness and completely no-sell it.<br /> <br /> The low values like 3-4...no that's never going to be a big epic reveal that everyone around the table cheers for, but...so? When was the last time someone was like &quot;Ah, but you forget, my ultimate move! Excellent Strike!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T13:42:32-07:00","id":1387067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387026#post1387026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying low level Hardness is useless, but in the grand scheme of things, it feels like people are overselling how useful it is in context of everything else going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking for myself that was not my intention.<br /> It's a weak effect that you probably gained as a freebie with bonus soak that might stop you losing a health level but mostly it's like a weapon tag, a system hook that you could tie into an interesting effect but in it's unaugmented state you might forget it exists. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T16:15:03-07:00","id":1387115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387065#post1387065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you intentionally built and played your character to have an Artifact 5 absolutely legendary bulwark that's given you a reputation of being unkillable then that's kind of on you, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Exalted, how is it &quot;on me,&quot; for making a character that's good at something to an epic degree? That's what the game tells me to make. I'm not going against the intentions of the game making a character like that. We're supposed to make characters with world changing epic power. Other characters trying to stop our characters is one of the main conflicts built into the concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean if the Unconquered Sun comes down to Creation, levels the Godspear of All-Searing Noon on me and says &quot;Come, I offer a challenge, defeat me in single combat and you shall have the Throne of Heaven.&quot; I'm not ever going to take him up on that one. </div> </div> </div>Mastering an Artifact 5 weapon's evocation's doesn't turn you into the Unconquered Sun in terms of what level of threat you are.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, you and I are squishy mortals. We're not Exalted. We're not part of a setting where not even the most powerful of the gods is beyond getting his face punched in by a potent enough and pissed off enough Exalt, should he decide to issue that sort of challenge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I have Hardness 5 that means an enemy with 5i isn't going to attack me with their decisive, they're going to pick somebody else or they're going to wither me. </div> </div> </div>Most likely they're going to wither anyway because 5i has poor odds of doing much, or they're so desperate that it's a last parting shot; though they might go for a gambit in that situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...are probably not going to bother without a good reason. </div> </div> </div>And there's a plethora of good reasons out there for the ST to use so that the players don't feel screwed out of using their cool toys.<br /> <br /> Like, the Wyld Hunt isn't going to sit around saying, &quot;You know that Anathema that's said to have mastered the long lost Direlance of Doom? Lets just ignore them for a few years so they can get even more powerful before we attack.&quot;<br /> <br /> The setting is built to promote conflict (yes not just combat, but the thread's about a combat mechanic), not passivity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as resources go, motes are less important than health levels. You don't die when you run out of motes, you don't take a -4 penalty to all actions when you're almost out of motes. If you have to go into battle with one mote left, or one health level left, you know which one you're taking. </div> </div> </div>Sure, but going into a fight with Ligier with 1m and full health is still a really shitty situation to be in.<br /> <br /> But the spectrum between the extremes isn't as straightforward. If you could pick those two, or being down 1 HL and 3/4 of your motes... having some juice left for Charms might be worth that -0 box being gone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also it requires you to dodge the attack, which you can't actually ensure without a bunch of motes being spent. </div> </div> </div>Besides a bunch of stuff that comes down to, &quot;A Charm that you'd use 80% of the time and a Charm that you'd use 20% of the time, are both Charms you don't use 100% of the time, so isn't that really the same thing?&quot;<br /> <br /> You can ensure without spending any motes, because Solar Dodge, even if that's not all that smart. But the ability to mix motes and initiative to drop their odds to highly improbable should be good enough even if it's not 100%. A Evasion of 9 is all you need to drop a Blood-Ape to &lt; 1% odds of being able to hit you without spending all the way to get to 12 just to make it truly impossible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, low-level hardness is not universally insanely useful. </div> </div> </div>Nobody's asking it to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is a very big problem with Exalted not having a DMG. </div> </div> </div>Well, one is in the works. But since, to my understand, it's not actually going to change the rules, the issues with the usefulness of low Hardness aren't going to change even if there's better ST advice around it.<br /> <br /> What can the ST advice really amount to besides how to force situations where certain effects that don't normal shine as well as they should are particularly useful?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, the game kind of straight-up doesn't work if you don't play it like that. </div> </div> </div>My experience with the game doesn't really follow that at all. Hardness didn't come off terribly well, but the rest of the game didn't fall apart just because the NPCs weren't spamming low initiative decisive attacks all the time.<br /> <br /> If you mean something like, &quot;judge NPC actions more on what's appropriate to the character over what's optimal,&quot; yeah, I'd agree with that, I just don't see how spamming decisive attacks fits into that most of the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Invulnerable Skin of Bronze is a problem spell, in my opinion. </div> </div> </div>While that may be the case the point of 6 + Essence Hardness for the day, is something people are going to take over 4 Hardness for a tick, if they want to really use Hardness to shape the flow of combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless the ST just thinks to themself &quot;Jame's character has Durability of Oak, which means that if this 6i bloodape attacks her, James can just activate that charm reflexively and negate it, which means I won't do that.&quot; which is probably too much tactical thinking on the ST's part, and maybe doesn't jive that well with the setting even. Unless this bloodape has some intel on the character that they can make their body like diamond, so if you're going to hit you'd better hit hard. </div> </div> </div>The problem that it doesn't take this at all.<br /> <br /> The ST just has to go, &quot;Well, you need at least 20 dice of decisive damage to put serious hurt on a normal human health track, so the Blood-Ape is going to wait until 10i before tossing a Principle of Motion double whammy on Jack's character, esp. since it can't do that too many times with the WP cost, it's not going to waste it on low damage attacks.&quot; The ST isn't trying to kill Jack's PC, and is unlikely to despite blowing past Hardness, the Blood-Ape is just trying to hit a human-shaped thing as hard as it normally takes to put a human-shaped thing down.<br /> <br /> Which is kinda the problem with Hardness, esp. at low levels. You don't need to even be thinking about it to make it inapplicable as the ST. The math of, &quot;this is the bar for an attack to seriously mess some one up if it rolls average,&quot; puts you past Hardness really easily, and most characters aren't sitting there going, &quot;I should try to death by 1,000 cuts this foe instead of trying my best to kill it ASAP.&quot;<br /> <br /> It also obviously goes against the intended flow of combat as intended to spam smaller attacks; even if the game is designed in a fashion where that's the best choice sometimes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The low values like 3-4...no that's never going to be a big epic reveal that everyone around the table cheers for, but...so? </div> </div> </div>That's kinda the point of the thread. Even if less &quot;everyone cheers,&quot; and more, &quot;there was a point in even having it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When was the last time someone was like &quot;Ah, but you forget, my ultimate move! Excellent Strike!&quot; </div> </div> </div>But that's not really what's low Hardness being useful is about.<br /> <br /> It's, &quot;Even at Essence 5, I still toss Excellent Strike into my attacks, because the nobody leaching off my 1s is worth the fractional difference between spending 3m on Excellency dice instead.&quot;<br /> <br /> While Durability of Oak Meditation has that kind of longevity in use, it's because of the damage reduction, not the Hardness (not even with Diamond-Body Prana boosting it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T18:19:44-07:00","id":1387138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387115#post1387115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's Exalted, how is it &quot;on me,&quot; for making a character that's good at something to an epic degree? That's what the game tells me to make. I'm not going against the intentions of the game making a character like that. We're supposed to make characters with world changing epic power. Other characters trying to stop our characters is one of the main conflicts built into the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree. I was just saying if you've made an effort to make sure everyone knows you can not be defeated in combat, that might lower the amount of people who are willing to pick a fight with you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387115#post1387115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most likely they're going to wither anyway because 5i has poor odds of doing much, or they're so desperate that it's a last parting shot; though they might go for a gambit in that situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I mean by changing how you play them makes hardness better or worse. When I have a group of bloodapes I'm not aiming to have them build up to 20i, which statistically is likely to kill a normal human. I'm looking to use them to inflict damage, which comes in either the form of motes, or especially health levels, or both ideally. The thing with a lot of antagonists though is, if you try to wait until they have 20i, they'll never launch decisives.<br /> <br /> If I want to inflict wounds, I'm going to have to launch from low initiative. If you launch with 6i though, you've got a pretty good chance of dealing 2-3L. If you're a blood ape and can flurry that into two attacks, even better. If every bloodape deals 2-3 damage before they die that's an absolute win. Now everyone is in their -1s or -2s, unless they have wound penalty ignoring magic, another piss-weak hit might drive one or two of them into their -4.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387115#post1387115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the ability to mix motes and initiative to drop their odds to highly improbable should be good enough even if it's not 100%. A Evasion of 9 is all you need to drop a Blood-Ape to &lt; 1% odds of being able to hit you without spending all the way to get to 12 just to make it truly impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so you're spending 2i for Reed in the Wind, and 4m for an excellency on the first attack, then 2i for Reed in the Wind, 4m for an excellency and 2m for Shadow Over Water, for a total of 4i and 10m. The resistance guy just spent 3 and negated both attacks. The excellency and Reed in the Wind are useful in more situations, but in that one Durability of Oak is better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387115#post1387115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While that may be the case the point of 6 + Essence Hardness for the day, is something people are going to take over 4 Hardness for a tick, if they want to really use Hardness to shape the flow of combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, people will often tend towards using overpowered combos if they exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387115#post1387115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is kinda the problem with Hardness, esp. at low levels. You don't need to even be thinking about it to make it inapplicable as the ST. The math of, &quot;this is the bar for an attack to seriously mess some one up if it rolls average,&quot; puts you past Hardness really easily, and most characters aren't sitting there going, &quot;I should try to death by 1,000 cuts this foe instead of trying my best to kill it ASAP.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The bloodape is not going to win this encounter. There is no universe where a small group of bloodapes annihilates the Solar's PCs unless they're already wounded/exhausted. The bloodape's goal here is not to win. Even in universe the bloodape's goal might not be to win, but even if it was that doesn't mean it's going to wait until it can kill a player in one shot before it tries to inflict damage.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that a bloodape should never launch withering strikes, there's plenty of reasons why it would. If it's crashed, obviously yes, it's going to wither. If it's sitting at 3i and all the Solars just launched decisive attacks, it might go for a crash and to end up going first next round. If it looks like it has a good opportunity to use Brutal Ape Pounce that could be another good reason.<br /> <br /> Depending on the exact context, it's also not looking to die with unspent willpower. If it dies with 4wp still left in the bank, that's a bad death, it did not put in it's full effort even when its life was on the line against a hated enemy, and most bloodapes don't last more than a few rounds in combat anyway. It might even go so far as to launch a decisive attack on round 1 with a willpower boosting both attacks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T18:47:43-07:00","id":1387148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387065#post1387065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you intentionally built and played your character to have an Artifact 5 absolutely legendary bulwark that's given you a reputation of being unkillable then that's kind of on you, isn't it? I mean if the Unconquered Sun comes down to Creation, levels the Godspear of All-Searing Noon on me and says &quot;Come, I offer a challenge, defeat me in single combat and you shall have the Throne of Heaven.&quot; I'm not ever going to take him up on that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be funny to have the Unconquered Sun do that in a game, the PCs all say &quot;Thanks, but we're good&quot;, and then Sol just peaces out back to heaven and the game continues as normal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For armor hardness I can see that, but the reflexive hardness not so much. &quot;Okay James, the 6i bloodape is going to flurry a pair of decisive attacks into you. You activate Durability of Oak? Okay they glance harmlessly off your iron-hard skin, no need to roll.&quot;<br /> <br /> Unless the ST just thinks to themself &quot;Jame's character has Durability of Oak, which means that if this 6i bloodape attacks her, James can just activate that charm reflexively and negate it, which means I won't do that.&quot; which is probably too much tactical thinking on the ST's part, and maybe doesn't jive that well with the setting even. Unless this bloodape has some intel on the character that they can make their body like diamond, so if you're going to hit you'd better hit hard. </div> </div> </div>Durability of Oak is definitely useful for this reason.<br /> <br /> But it's also probably easy to get disappointed by it, because it looks more useful than it is (and the flavortext sells it a bit too hard IMO).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T19:01:39-07:00","id":1387151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387148#post1387148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would be funny to have the Unconquered Sun do that in a game, the PCs all say &quot;Thanks, but we're good&quot;, and then Sol just peaces out back to heaven and the game continues as normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be hilarious if he then went on to try and goad them into it &quot;Okaaay, but it's reeeallly comfy. So comfy. I hate to give it up.&quot; and he's just like, pointedly not leaving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T00:05:46-07:00","id":1387198,"title":"","content":"Oh I also just realized that a lot of low Gardness effects don\u2019t care about your stats, or if they do it\u2019s stamina based. That alone could make it compare favourably to other option if your taking a low initiative attack. Your Evasion 2 ass isn\u2019t going to be able to boost your defense to 11 no matter what you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T01:04:19-07:00","id":1387203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387026#post1387026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fortunately the setting isn't meant to be full of perfectly intelligent and omniscient enemies. It feels very strange for this to be the response while praising the Blood Ape example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, summoned demons that live to commit violence and are notoriously single minded are probably the closest thing you are going to get to meat grinder enemies.<br /> <br /> Secondly, you don't have to be perfectly intelligent or omniscient to avoid the famous demi-god, wielding a six foot long legendary golden sword.<br /> <br /> What are you fighting?<br /> <br /> The local kingdoms are going to have spies.<br /> The Wyld Hunt has Sidereals.<br /> Lunars and Abyssals aren't renowned for their stupid decisions. <br /> <br /> You can fight things like walking volcanos and summoned demons forced into combat with you to wear you down. But most threats which are powerful enough to meaningfully challenge an Essence ~3 Solar with a mastered Artifact 5 weapon (keeping in mind you can only get an Artifact 5 weapon with ST permission) are smart enough to not want to walk into a meat grinder. <br /> <br /> Not to be rude, but I honestly don't see how you are trying to debate this. I'm happy to hear your point of view, and listen to reasons why characters in the setting would decide to face-tank your epic sword rather than avoid you or try to seperate you from the blade. But I can't think of any canon foe who would vaguely consider it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point is that if the player invests in being able to do X... they should get to do X, not be satisfied with everyone being too deterred that X will happen that it rarely ever does. </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but 3E isn't built that way.<br /> <br /> If you overspec for combat, you don't get dynamic combats between legendary creatures. If you want an exciting fight against a deadly Manticore you want Dex 3 Martial Arts 3 and two Charms. With Dex 5 Melee 5 and an entire Artifact 5 Evocation tree... you are going to breeze over 90% of antagonists. It's not even worth busting out the dice for. The story isn't &quot;do you win this epic combat&quot; but it becomes a One Punch Man &quot;you must struggle with the ennui of having no foes who can challenge you&quot;.<br /> <br /> Take an Artifact 3 with one or two Evocations if you want to &quot;do X&quot;. And rather than min-maxing X, put some Charms in Y and Z so you can do those as well so your ST isn't limited in the interesting stories they can present you with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-10-2020, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T04:22:20-07:00","id":1387244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387138#post1387138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just saying if you've made an effort to make sure everyone knows you can not be defeated in combat, that might lower the amount of people who are willing to pick a fight with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was never part of the example I made. It was &quot;but became famous,&quot; since it's pretty hard for you to be a world changing epic hero and people not notice if you main thing is a high powered magical item.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is what I mean by changing how you play them makes hardness better or worse. </div> </div> </div>It seems to mostly leave two situations:<br /> <br /> The ST makes low decisive attacks all the time, so everyone picks up enough Hardness to ignore them (which isn't hard if the bar is ~6i), and then any NPC worth fighting needs to be able to go against the group well enough that they actually have a shot at getting higher initiative for bigger decisive attacks.<br /> <br /> The same thing but you don't bother with the &quot;spamming low damage decisive attacks so everyone picks up Hardness to make those worthless&quot; and end up in the same place, leaving at least some change for low damage decisive attacks to even come up since everyone isn't taking Hardness as part of the OTB.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I have a group of bloodapes I'm not aiming to have them build up to 20i, which statistically is likely to kill a normal human. </div> </div> </div>My example was to get them to 10i.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm looking to use them to inflict damage, which comes in either the form of motes, or especially health levels, or both ideally. </div> </div> </div>Which means using enemies that can actually wither their opponents, or at least can get a decent JB roll if they're just going to decisive once before they're killed.<br /> <br /> If they spend all their time at low initiative, the PCs are just going to crash them before they can go, and then never get to decisive anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, so you're spending 2i for Reed in the Wind, and 4m for an excellency on the first attack, then 2i for Reed in the Wind, 4m for an excellency and 2m for Shadow Over Water, for a total of 4i and 10m. The resistance guy just spent 3 and negated both attacks. The excellency and Reed in the Wind are useful in more situations, but in that one Durability of Oak is better. </div> </div> </div>Except Principle of Motion doesn't have the same protections that the Solar flurry Charms do. If the Blood-Ape misses the first attack, they Crash before the second one, and then the second one can't be decisive. So it's 2i and 4m to avoid any decisive damage, and Crash the Blood-Ape in the process; if you even feel like lowering the odds that much since 2i and 2m would leave you unscathed the vast majority of the time. And we're completely skipping that you can Stunt Evasion, but not Hardness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, people will often tend towards using overpowered combos if they exist. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how the Hardness there is overpowered. Even if you consider the cost/benefit of the spell overpowered compared to the cost/benefit of medium and heavy Artifact armor, the numbers they grant are on par with each other. A Sorcerer with ISoB as a control spell isn't running around with more Hardness than other routes can get you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The bloodape's goal here is not to win. Even in universe the bloodape's goal might not be to win, but even if it was that doesn't mean it's going to wait until it can kill a player in one shot before it tries to inflict damage. </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about waiting until it can kill a PC Exalted. I'm talking about waiting until it could kill a normal mortal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387203#post1387203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firstly, summoned demons that live to commit violence and are notoriously single minded are probably the closest thing you are going to get to meat grinder enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're mixing examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Secondly, you don't have to be perfectly intelligent or omniscient to avoid the famous demi-god, wielding a six foot long legendary golden sword. </div> </div> </div>Well, you have to be if you're going to avoid them and stop them somehow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not to be rude, but I honestly don't see how you are trying to debate this. </div> </div> </div>Well, I expect the debate to not be as needlessly hyperbolic as you're being. Mastering a 5 dot Artifact weapon is a very powerful thing to do, but it's not an instant &quot;I Win&quot; button, nor does it mean you're an overspeced combat min-maxed character builder. Evocations for them are generally more powerful, but in practice like mastering a Martial Arts style: you have to fight in a specific way to really get your XP's worth, which means having exploitable weaknesses beyond &quot;sorry you don't get to use your expensive toy because I can't be bothered to have anyone fight you.&quot; <br /> <br /> If your foe has mastered Soulfarer... raise an army of golems or undead, and then give them some sorcery (or at least anti-sorcery) back up. Without enemies with souls, or blood, and esp. ones with decent Hardness, someone using Soulfarer can end up doing some damage to themselves and is mostly going to be forced to fight like a sorcerer than someone with a giant magical ax.<br /> <br /> Your choices are not binary like you're making them out to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The story isn't &quot;do you win this epic combat&quot; but it becomes a One Punch Man &quot;you must struggle with the ennui of having no foes who can challenge you&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I don't buy that at all... esp. since you yourself admitted that there's that 10% to challenge you (and some of them invariably will).<br /> <br /> As well, the fact that you're a high combat spec Solar with a full Evocation tree mastered doesn't mean fights can't be challenging even if you're going to win them. Saitama's ennui isn't that he always wins, but that the fights aren't fun because he wins with one punch (except the few times he actually needs to fight harder even if they don't last). There's plenty in the setting for putting up a bigger fight than that to a combat heavy Solar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T04:48:10-07:00","id":1387249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1386930#post1386930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had a 5 dot Artifact, mastered all the Evocations, but became famous for it and I mostly use it by scaring away enemies from fighting me <b>unless they can manipulate the situation to keep my Artifact out of it</b>, then... I'm using it but it feels pretty weak.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387244#post1387244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I expect the debate to not be as needlessly hyperbolic as you're being. Mastering a 5 dot Artifact weapon is a very powerful thing to do, but it's not an instant &quot;I Win&quot; button, nor does it mean you're an overspeced combat min-maxed character builder. Evocations for them are generally more powerful, but in practice like mastering a Martial Arts style: you have to fight in a specific way to really get your XP's worth, which means having exploitable weaknesses beyond &quot;sorry you don't get to use your expensive toy because I can't be bothered to have anyone fight you.&quot; <br /> <br /> <b>If your foe has mastered Soulfarer...</b> raise an army of golems or undead, and then give them some sorcery (or at least anti-sorcery) back up. Without enemies with souls, or blood, and esp. ones with decent Hardness, someone using Soulfarer can end up doing some damage to themselves and is mostly going to be forced to fight like a sorcerer than someone with a giant magical ax.<br /> <br /> Your choices are not binary like you're making them out to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have <i>no idea</i> what your argument is, or how to help you to enjoy the hardness mechanic, so I'm going to bow out here. <br /> <br /> I think the Hardness mechanic is fine. Agree to disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-10-2020, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T06:28:01-07:00","id":1387258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387244#post1387244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't buy that at all... esp. since you yourself admitted that there's that 10% to challenge you (and some of them invariably will).<br /> <br /> As well, the fact that you're a high combat spec Solar with a full Evocation tree mastered doesn't mean fights can't be challenging even if you're going to win them. Saitama's ennui isn't that he always wins, but that the fights aren't fun because he wins with one punch (except the few times he actually needs to fight harder even if they don't last). There's plenty in the setting for putting up a bigger fight than that to a combat heavy Solar</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been discussed at greater length in other threads. The issue is not literally that no foes exist that can challenge the Solar. Rather the problem is that against almost every one of these foes, the fight will take a long time to run and not be particularly fun. Because of various features of the setting, fights between weaker foes and weaker foes are shorter, easier to run, and more fun.<br /> <br /> The easiest fight for the DM to set up in terms of Storytelling is one solar vs. many DBs, because there's plenty of DBs around Creation and they like to gang up on Solars. But this is also one of the worst fights to run because there are multiple combatants, they have many different powers, and their motes need to be tracked. It will take ages and require lots of math. <br /> <br /> Not all powerful foes have all the same problems but almost all of them have some.<br /> <br /> Even if you do enjoy these fights, they will still probably take a lot of time, and so there can't be too many of them during a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T11:12:14-07:00","id":1387299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387244#post1387244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was never part of the example I made. It was &quot;but became famous,&quot; since it's pretty hard for you to be a world changing epic hero and people not notice if you main thing is a high powered magical item.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case you should maybe make an effort not to become famous, as especially for Solars that's incredibly dangerous. When my DB ascends to the throne and becomes Empress, traveling around in a carriage with the rest off my Essence 4-5 hearth, and bearing my personal mon I expect that banditry will not concern me unless they have some reason to think they have a chance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387244#post1387244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ST makes low decisive attacks all the time, so everyone picks up enough Hardness to ignore them (which isn't hard if the bar is ~6i), and then any NPC worth fighting needs to be able to go against the group well enough that they actually have a shot at getting higher initiative for bigger decisive attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not hard to get that kind of hardness, but it's also not effortless. Seeing and fighting dematerialized spirits isn't hard, resisting extreme environments isn't hard, protecting your character from the mutating powers of the Wyld isn't hard, but how many characters do you know that can't do at least one of those things? There's a huge number of things in Exalted that are good to be able to do, but the only way you're going to grab them all is if you sacrifice a lot of other parts of your character.<br /> <br /> That's not even considering how badly your character can get messed up if they neglect social defenses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387244#post1387244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they spend all their time at low initiative, the PCs are just going to crash them before they can go, and then never get to decisive anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience the PCs consistently wither any enemies that get high initiative, stopping them from ever being in a position to launch decisive attacks from high initiative. If I want to actually inflict some health level damage on my PCs I'm going to have to start the fight outnumbering them, and then whoever doesn't get crashed on round 1 fires off their decisive attacks. The apes who got crashed turn 1, they can use their actions to wither the PCs.<br /> <br /> Five initiative attacks do damage, sometimes zero damage, sometimes five even, but they'll always do more lasting damage than a withering attack. Erymanthus have 4 parry, unboostable by anything but Willpower, and 7 soak. They have a hard time holding on to the initiative that they have. So do lots of other things, like claw striders. They have Evasion 4 and 7 soak, but they also have a 12 die attack that gets 3 automatic successes if there's at least 3 other claw striders around, which gives them an average attack roll of 9, before willpower.<br /> <br /> <br /> If I'm launching a claw strider ambush on the PCs in the depths of a super deadly jungle my strategy is to have the clawstriders charge in with pack tactics, but with a join battle pool of only 4 dice they're not likely to be going first. The ones who roll lucky and get a few successes on that JB roll are going to be crashed into the ground by the PCs who rolled well and went before them, so all I'm left with is a bunch of crashed clawstriders, and any who are still around are the ones who didn't roll so hot on their four dice, so probably looking at base initiative.<br /> <br /> In that case as the round progresses I'm going to be launching those 3i clawstrider's decisive attacks, spending a willpower on the attack roll and a willpower to boost their damage to 6i with Pack Hunting to get in some rakes before they all die. If I don't do that, and try to wither, I'm either trying to hit with a low accuracy bite, or a low damage claw, even if I do hit with that all the PCs just launched their withering attacks with crash bonus, none of them are in range of being crashed themselves.<br /> <br /> Then the round resets and the PCs are looking at a board with a bunch of crashed claw striders who aren't threats at all, and a few who have maybe some actually decently deadly initiative. Well THAT won't do, so now the claw striders who have deadly initiative get withered and probably even crashed under the weight of so many attacks. The the striders go, all crashed now trying to wither PCs who have like literally 40 initiative, and the round resets, and the PCs all launch their finishers to annihilate all but a few of the striders, or maybe use some decisive charms to slay them all. The combat is over either way because two clawstriders who are deeply crashed aren't really worth playing out anymore, assuming they don't just flee after the massacre of their fellows.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If I get some PCs into their -1s though by dealing just two levels of lethal damage, that damage lasts <i>days. </i>If I can subsequently deal damage into their -2 health levels it could last <i>weeks. </i>In that period of time they might get into another fight, with a few other little chips of damage where they might not even come out ahead. The kinds of enemies the Solars face often have thousands, or even millions of individuals fighting for them, chances are good they're going to run into more than a few.<br /> <br /> You might say &quot;Okay, but then they'll just get healing charms, or someone will get medicine charms and they'll heal it all up in a day.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yep. Good. Now the guy playing the Supernal Medicine uber-doctor becomes a cornerstone of the circle's success. Now just as much as the Dawn annihilates their powerful enemies, and the Zenith squares off against the silver tongued fey monsters, the Twilight is keeping everyone from being run ragged and bloody by their myriad foes. Or nobody wants to do that and they actually have to make a difficult choice if they should push on and go delving into that tomb to stop a horrible infernal cult from summoning yet more demons, or if they need to rest and hope that they can take whatever comes out of there when they get back to 100%.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387244#post1387244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except Principle of Motion doesn't have the same protections that the Solar flurry Charms do. If the Blood-Ape misses the first attack, they Crash before the second one, and then the second one can't be decisive. So it's 2i and 4m to avoid any decisive damage, and Crash the Blood-Ape in the process; if you even feel like lowering the odds that much since 2i and 2m would leave you unscathed the vast majority of the time. And we're completely skipping that you can Stunt Evasion, but not Hardness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if they were at 3i before and not 4+. Plus you're still comparing 2i and 4m to 3m, plus the application of multiple dodge charms, one of which has a minimum ability of 4, to one half of one Resistance 2 charm. If you're that good at dodging, then yeah, use dodge. If you have Resistance 2 and Dodge 0, maybe consider using DoOM instead?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387244#post1387244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how the Hardness there is overpowered. Even if you consider the cost/benefit of the spell overpowered compared to the cost/benefit of medium and heavy Artifact armor, the numbers they grant are on par with each other. A Sorcerer with ISoB as a control spell isn't running around with more Hardness than other routes can get you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Overpowered and broken are two different but related concepts. My new Melee charm which is exactly like Excellent Strike in every way except it costs 2 motes and has the Mute keyword isn't breaking the game, but it's overpowered compared to the rest of your options. ISoS gives you +6 soak that stacks with armor, and hardness almost equal to medium artifact armor, with no mobility penalty, plus 3 new charms, plus immunity to contact poisons, and it doesn't even have as much of an instant indicator that you're an exalt. IN ADDITION to the bonus that if you're unarmored those soak and hardness bonuses climb based on your essence.<br /> <br /> PLUS if you're getting this with your sorcery, which you are if it's your control spell, it comes with being able to do sorcerous workings, counterspell other sorcerer's spells, distort made spells, and gives access to special merits through your sorcerous initiation.<br /> <br /> That's pretty damn good for one Occult 3 charm with no prerequisites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T15:25:33-07:00","id":1387345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387249#post1387249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have <i>no idea</i> what your argument is,..</div> </div> </div> </div>Of what you highlighted? What I explicitly said: mastering a 5 dot Artifact isn't a &quot;Win Button,&quot; that gives your opponents a binary choice of, &quot;charge into the meat grinder,&quot; or, &quot;avoid until you can remove the Artifact from play.&quot; Learning about the history of Soulfarer provides an obvious strategy to take Soulfarer's master head on, without letting Soulfarer become a meat grinder. Maybe you win, probably Soulfarer's master still wins (Soulfarer being used to boost sorcery is still really powerful even if you're not getting as much out of it as you could if you were fighting opponents it prefers), but it means there's a challenging and interesting fight there; one that's not so lopsided only &quot;idiots&quot; would take it on as you suggested earlier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...or how to help you to enjoy the hardness mechanic,.. </div> </div> </div>I'll enjoy the Hardness mechanic when either (preferably both):<br /> <br /> 1) Its descriptive purpose and mechanical effect are actually in-line with each other; including costs.<br /> <br /> 2) The way to enjoy it doesn't entail system mastery based meta logic such as what DrLoveMonkey is illustrating.<br /> <br /> What seems to have kicked off about half of this thread's discussion, is my statement that #2 there might be why low Hardness if functional, but why it isn't fun to a lot of people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387258#post1387258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather the problem is that against almost every one of these foes, the fight will take a long time to run and not be particularly fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why Crucible of Legend and Exalted: Essence are getting made.<br /> <br /> But it remains a lackluster response to, &quot;I bought this for my character because I want to use it actively, not so that it sits around only being 'used' by causing the situation it's for to never come up.&quot;<br /> <br /> Esp. since unlike a high level Artifact, the low Hardness utility issues crop up very quickly for Exalts. And worse, the best utility for Hardness is... to make those weaker foes less interesting to fight, because it removes their main ability to be a significant threat: spamming low damage decisive attacks before they lose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because of various features of the setting, fights between weaker foes and weaker foes are shorter, easier to run, and more fun. </div> </div> </div>System not setting?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if you do enjoy these fights, they will still probably take a lot of time, and so there can't be too many of them during a game. </div> </div> </div>Who said there need to be more than a few? There just needs to be enough for combat heavy characters to feel like there was a point in being a combat heavy character instead of constantly fighting things you barely need to bust out Charms against.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387299#post1387299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When my DB ascends to the throne and becomes Empress, traveling around in a carriage with the rest off my Essence 4-5 hearth, and bearing my personal mon I expect that banditry will not concern me unless they have some reason to think they have a chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, but do you seriously expect that your ST isn't (assuming that don't consider winning the throne a good place to end the chronicle) going to have the PCs attacked sometimes despite (or more likely because of) this? None of the other heavier hitter Dragbonbloods are going to try to assassinate you all under the guise of bandits? No Lunars are going to try to take you out? Etc.<br /> <br /> As a player.. don't you want that sort of thing to happen in a game where you fought for the throne and won? You didn't take the throne to sit back and not-roll Bureaucracy all day, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not hard to get that kind of hardness, but it's also not effortless. </div> </div> </div>A major difference here is what Lioness and I both pointed out: Hardness is usually a package deal with other thing.<br /> <br /> There are multiple ways to get Hardness, unlike a lot of other effects. A Martial Arts Supernal Dawn (there's three that have a Hardness power in the core book alone), a Resistance Supernal Zenith, a Twilight non-sorcerer via Anima, a Night whatever with light Artifact armor that's got some sneaky Evocation tree to it, and an Eclipse Sorcerer can all access Hardness.<br /> <br /> You don't have to go dipping around outside of your character focus to have Hardness effects unlike a lot of bread and butter effects you're talking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In my experience the PCs consistently wither any enemies that get high initiative, stopping them from ever being in a position to launch decisive attacks from high initiative. </div> </div> </div>Maybe... send more challenging enemies after them? Take advantage of the BG mechanics (esp. for enemies that don't have Charms to consider)? There's options here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...maybe consider using DoOM instead? </div> </div> </div>Will you please stop posting like I'm trying to shit on DoOM as a Charm?<br /> <br /> You don't need to defend it, I'm not calling it a bad Charm. I am saying the Hardness part of it isn't what makes it such a solid Charm, because the thread's about Hardness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Overpowered and broken are two different but related concepts. </div> </div> </div>Similarly, can you please stop posting like I'm trying to defend ISoB? I'm saying the Hardness bonus from it isn't out of place for the system, even if the spells gives way too much stuff, because again, the thread is about Hardness.<br /> <br /> I'm aware I've brought up other things, but they're in comparison to Hardness to judge it's utility, not to pick fights about if this Charm is good enough, or if that spell is bad via whichever adjective you want to apply.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T16:59:00-07:00","id":1387362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387345#post1387345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, but do you seriously expect that your ST isn't (assuming that don't consider winning the throne a good place to end the chronicle) going to have the PCs attacked sometimes despite (or more likely because of) this? None of the other heavier hitter Dragbonbloods are going to try to assassinate you all under the guise of bandits? No Lunars are going to try to take you out? Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but if we get to that point in the game we might have moved past spending a lot of time on drastically weaker foes than the circle started out facing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387345#post1387345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are multiple ways to get Hardness, unlike a lot of other effects. A Martial Arts Supernal Dawn (there's three that have a Hardness power in the core book alone), a Resistance Supernal Zenith, a Twilight non-sorcerer via Anima, a Night whatever with light Artifact armor that's got some sneaky Evocation tree to it, and an Eclipse Sorcerer can all access Hardness.<br /> <br /> You don't have to go dipping around outside of your character focus to have Hardness effects unlike a lot of bread and butter effects you're talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand why that makes Hardness bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387345#post1387345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe... send more challenging enemies after them? Take advantage of the BG mechanics (esp. for enemies that don't have Charms to consider)? There's options here.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some problems with that. One is that if you built a bunch of Solars to be really badass by Solar standards, there's not a lot of foes in the world who can meaningfully challenge them without outnumbering them. Not only in the setting but also in the published materials. The corebook, and Adversaries of the Righteous, and Hundred Devil Night Parade are all filled to bursting with antagonists like Steel Eaters, Greenmaws, Aughdeighe, Jungle Stalkers or whatever, there's literally dozens of them.<br /> <br /> Putting them in a battlegroup doesn't always help either, sometimes it's simply not appropriate to have them form a battlegroup, and most of the time it's only going to result in the PCs smashing it to pieces round 1 before it even acts, and well before it can crash somebody, and then attack again to deal real damage.<br /> <br /> It's also not terrible design, because if the players all built themselves to be some of the greatest warriors of the human race, the number of creatures that can fight them without outnumbering them should be small.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387345#post1387345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need to defend it, I'm not calling it a bad Charm. I am saying the Hardness part of it isn't what makes it such a solid Charm, because the thread's about Hardness.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Hardness part is useful. If you're going to eat a 6i attack or less, and especially if you're going to eat multiples of them on a single tick, for 3m it keeps you perfectly safe. It's not a particularly powerful effect, but it's also not a particularly powerful charm either. Low Hardness values aren't supposed to feel that useful, because, just as you say, they're so often package deals with other things, and don't block big effects that your character would die to in one shot. Although if you're already in your -4s and your enemy is throwing one last desperate 5i strike at you to kill you it could save your life.<br /> <br /> Sight Without Eyes from Archery's base effect is useless if your ST never uses environmental penalties based on vision conditions, and if they don't use cover even the Essence 3+ power is worthless. It doesn't make Sight Without Eyes a bad charm, there's some Storytellers out there that will have your character eating visual penalties every other combat, sometimes absolutely crippling ones up to -5, and ignoring them for one mote is amazing. Other Storytellers completely forget that environmental penalties as a whole are even a thing, and it's never rainy, or stormy, or foggy, or slick, or anything, and those charms are garbage because of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387345#post1387345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, can you please stop posting like I'm trying to defend ISoB? I'm saying the Hardness bonus from it isn't out of place for the system, even if the spells gives way too much stuff, because again, the thread is about Hardness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so what if ISoB was just a charm with the same effects, would that be overpowered compared to other charms? A charm with Resistance 3, Essence 1, no prerequisites, no cost, 24 hour duration, provides 6 Hardness and +6 natural soak, and is less suspicious than artifact armor. Is there any charm that grants Hardness that's that too good? Diamond Body Prana is Resistance 4, Essence 2, is four charms deep into its tree, is scenelong, provides variable resistance with an average of 8, maximum 5 hardness, is incompatible with armor, and only lasts for a scene.<br /> <br /> Your original question was &quot;Why would you take 4(which is effectively 6) Hardness for a tick when you could take 6 Hardness for the whole day?&quot; the reason is you wouldn't, you would absolutely always take ISoB because it's overpowered for the cost you pay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T17:33:49-07:00","id":1387370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387362#post1387362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but if we get to that point in the game we might have moved past spending a lot of time on drastically weaker foes than the circle started out facing.</div> </div> </div> </div>But so much of this tangent is, basically, &quot;Hardness is useful even at low levels because you should never move past the weaker foes that you started facing.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't understand why that makes Hardness bad. </div> </div> </div>By itself, it doesn't. It just makes the argument that getting Hardness takes &quot;effort&quot; less compelling.<br /> <br /> How it decreases the utility of Hardness, is that it pushes low damage decisive attacks outside of the ST's toolkit for making minor encounters have any point to them. The only way to make encounters interesting is if the enemies have a decent chance of making decisive attacks that will defeat Hardness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One is that if you built a bunch of Solars to be really badass by Solar standards, there's not a lot of foes in the world who can meaningfully challenge them without outnumbering them. </div> </div> </div>In my experience if the group make as a bunch of combat heavy characters, they want to have fun challenging fights with those foes that can make it fun and challenging (I never said taking outnumbering them off the table as part of that).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Low Hardness values aren't supposed to feel that useful,... </div> </div> </div>That's... basically the whole issue. They should feel useful, even if they're not big exciting effects. Excellent Strike might not be exciting, but it's useful. It's useful throughout the game. DoOM's damage reducing aspect isn't exciting, but it's useful, and useful throughout the game. DoOM's Hardness effect is much more limited in usefulness and doesn't hold up as time goes on.<br /> <br /> And that's how most Hardness packages end up. They're useful when you get them, which is nice, but the lower the level, the faster you ever actively use them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...is useless if your ST never uses... </div> </div> </div>Any argument that needs to be based on this sort of condition is rather obnoxiously bad faith. Whataboutism isn't productive discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, so what if ISoB was just a charm with the same effects, would that be overpowered compared to other charms? </div> </div> </div><b>For the purposes of this thread, I DON'T GIVE A SHIT.</b><br /> <br /> Again, the Whataboutism is pointless at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T19:11:26-07:00","id":1387391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387370#post1387370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But so much of this tangent is, basically, &quot;Hardness is useful even at low levels because you should never move past the weaker foes that you started facing.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I actually agree. I concede the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387370#post1387370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How it decreases the utility of Hardness, is that it pushes low damage decisive attacks outside of the ST's toolkit for making minor encounters have any point to them. The only way to make encounters interesting is if the enemies have a decent chance of making decisive attacks that will defeat Hardness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if every PC actually has hardness. It comes with a lot of stuff but not everyone gets it automatically. After a few days of being worn down by foes who keep nibbling away at the one guy who doesn't have Hardness 7+ he might get the idea that Hardness is actually saving everyone else's butt, and needs to get some himself.<br /> <br /> Or if by some miracle one of the PCs gets crashed and loses their hardness, only to have enemies wolf-pack all over them, the Twilight might think &quot;Oh thank god my Hardness works in crash.&quot; and the crashed guy is thinking &quot;Oh god, get my initiative back, I need my damn Hardness again.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387370#post1387370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my experience if the group make as a bunch of combat heavy characters, they want to have fun challenging fights with those foes that can make it fun and challenging (I never said taking outnumbering them off the table as part of that).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but how are you going to take enemies like claw striders and make them dangerous to PCs if those PCs are hellbent on never letting those striders get more than 3 initiative? How do you get them to a position where they both have high initiative, and go before the PCs so they won't get shut down before the PCs kill their combat momentum? Or just kill them with their decisive attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387370#post1387370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's... basically the whole issue. They should feel useful, even if they're not big exciting effects. Excellent Strike might not be exciting, but it's useful. It's useful throughout the game. DoOM's damage reducing aspect isn't exciting, but it's useful, and useful throughout the game. DoOM's Hardness effect is much more limited in usefulness and doesn't hold up as time goes on.</div> </div> </div> </div>DoOM's Hardness effect can be useful at any point in the game, as long as enemies are still using low initiative attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387370#post1387370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any argument that needs to be based on this sort of condition is rather obnoxiously bad faith. Whataboutism isn't productive discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not suggesting &quot;you think Sight Without Eyes is fine but sources of Hardness 5 are bad and how about you explain that to me then?&quot; I'm saying it's up to you and your Storyteller to make your character's abilities feel useful. If you're really excited about the idea that your Twilight anima banner can automatically deflect any low-powered serious attack against you, then your Storyteller should involve that in the game, even if they otherwise wouldn't, which I think they should anyway.<br /> <br /> If I had a character that I'm really excited about who had the power to absorb any poison he was inflicted with, and then turn around and use it myself on my own attacks, that's something that should come up a lot through the course of the story. Nothing at all in the game suggests that Storytellers should use poison constantly, in fact I'm pretty sure I've played entire campaigns where poison wasn't used a single time. That player might come out of the other side of that campaign thinking that power is utterly useless in its niche, but really it's just a failure to communicate to the ST that's something they really wanted, or for the ST to act on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387370#post1387370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>For the purposes of this thread, I DON'T GIVE A SHIT.</b><br /> <br /> Again, the Whataboutism is pointless at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, explain to me what you meant by this then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387026#post1387026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never seen anyone that wants to use Hardness this way stick to low levels of Hardness. You can pick up heavy Artifact armor for the same price. You can go the Sorcery route and start roughly on par with medium Artifact and get up to on par with heavy as your Essence goes up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because to me, it seems like you were asking what's the point of Hardness 4 when you could so easily just get Hardness 6 for a whole day for free. The answer is you should not so easily be able to get Hardness 6 for a whole day for free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T20:47:04-07:00","id":1387402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387391#post1387391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if every PC actually has hardness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the spread I cited earlier was actually my second 3e game's PCs... we all started with access to Hardness without even trying to specifically do that. It's literally something we stumbled into (though the fact that one of the Solar Castes get access for free does help that happen). Though our Tiger stylist's Hardness was a joke (we house ruled Celestial Tiger Hide to grant 3 or Essence whichever is higher Hardness instead of just Essence).<br /> <br /> Yes, not everyone is going to have Hardness, but then again, the NPCs ganging up on the characters without it (esp. without obvious sources of it like Charms) is a bit much. A bunch of Claws Striders aren't going to know that normal steel armor and magical armor are going to be different when they make decisive attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It comes with a lot of stuff but not everyone gets it automatically. After a few days of being worn down by foes who keep nibbling away at the one guy who doesn't have Hardness 7+ he might get the idea that Hardness is actually saving everyone else's butt, and needs to get some himself. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but that's also a really unfun situation for a lot of players when the ST keeps putting the group in a situation that's a grind for them, and a breeze for everyone else (assuming this even happens because, say, the character without access to Hardness didn't dip heavily into having high DV to avoid getting hit in the first place, since the game does say you should try to buy some defense even if you're not going to layer on lots of them).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, but how are you going to take enemies like claw striders and make them dangerous to PCs if those PCs are hellbent on never letting those striders get more than 3 initiative? </div> </div> </div>If I have to use claws striders instead of all of the other things I could pick instead?<br /> <br /> Not use the core book stat block. They're going to face a large pack of claw striders breed by an NPC in the past to be even nastier, that can operate as a Size 3 Elite Drill BG with higher baseline stats on top of it, with a non-QC &quot;alpha&quot; strider that can give orders to the pack, and 2-3 striders looking to be the next alpha, and all of them have increased stats as well. Just like if my group's PC are tearing apart militia stack block mortal troops, my answer doesn't have to be tossing in more and more and more militia troops when I can pick more potent troops, use BGs and commanders, and so on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or just kill them with their decisive attacks. </div> </div> </div>If we're talking about a combat heavy Solar group... this is pretty damned hard to do even if they get enough initiative to threaten it. It just means the PCs are going to toss a motes in defense that they wouldn't against withering attacks or low damage decisive attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> DoOM's Hardness effect can be useful at any point in the game, as long as enemies are still using low initiative attacks. </div> </div> </div>Considering having things like Glorious Solar Plate or Aegis of Invincible Might are there for Resistance Solars to grab? I'd say they have better Hardness options that makes DoOM's Hardness less and less appealing as time goes by.<br /> <br /> It's not just, &quot;as long as enemies are still using low initiative attacks,&quot; but also, &quot;as long as you never buy anything that can get you significantly better boosts too.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm saying it's up to you and your Storyteller to make your character's abilities feel useful. </div> </div> </div>And the game itself is still a factor in this. If the game forces us to have characters act in a specific - frequently uncharacteristic - way just to make low Hardness feel useful... we're allowed to say the system is the problem. Otherwise what's the point of the system exactly?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you're really excited about the idea that your Twilight anima banner can automatically deflect any low-powered serious attack against you, then your Storyteller should involve that in the game, even if they otherwise wouldn't, which I think they should anyway. </div> </div> </div>And yet, I find myself repeating that I'm not saying low damage decisive attacks should never happen. I'm saying they shouldn't be the required way lower tier enemies operate to matter, and once you cut out that mentality... it's a much rarer circumstance even if it will still happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, explain to me what you meant by this then.<br /> <br /> Because to me, it seems like you were asking what's the point of Hardness 4 when you could so easily just get Hardness 6 for a whole day for free. The answer is you should not so easily be able to get Hardness 6 for a whole day for free. </div> </div> </div>Because you've cut out the context of what that was a response to.<br /> <br /> The context was that &quot;having Hardness is fun because you reshape how combat needs to be fought.&quot; I was responding that anyone that I've ever seen that could be described as having that mentality, would be jumping for higher Hardness sources than Artifact light armor, Twilight Anima, or DoOM.<br /> <br /> I'm not asking what the point of Hardness 4 for a tick is when you can have Hardness 6 for a day. I'm asking if a character is trying to make Hardness a major part of their character's tactics, why are they stopping at low Hardness?<br /> <br /> To which the answer is, &quot;They shouldn't be.&quot; There's nothing wrong with jumping for better Hardness options just like any other thing your character might make a big part of your character's aptitudes, even if one official option among many others is particularly powerful/cheap.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T21:48:45-07:00","id":1387410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387402#post1387402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, not everyone is going to have Hardness, but then again, the NPCs ganging up on the characters without it (esp. without obvious sources of it like Charms) is a bit much. A bunch of Claws Striders aren't going to know that normal steel armor and magical armor are going to be different when they make decisive attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>The withering/decisive divide isn't actually an in-character knowledge divide though, it's an out of character narrative resource. The claw striders might not know the difference between magical armor and mundane armor, armor is armor, but their attacks against the guy who's armor would no-sell them with its artifact awesomeness more often end up as withering attacks, and the ones against guys who's armor doesn't magically protect them so well end up getting cut.<br /> <br /> I, the Storyteller, choose if the attack's success will end in a wound or a desperate scramble to keep the jaws from doing more than a superficial bruise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387402#post1387402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but that's also a really unfun situation for a lot of players when the ST keeps putting the group in a situation that's a grind for them, and a breeze for everyone else (assuming this even happens because, say, the character without access to Hardness didn't dip heavily into having high DV to avoid getting hit in the first place, since the game does say you should try to buy some defense even if you're not going to layer on lots of them).</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much recommend that if players want to make a combat character who doesn't invest in Soak and Hardness that they should absolutely invest in high Defense. Some characters have enemy attacks plink off them, or force them to make withering attacks because they still aren't over their hardness, and other characters just have crazy Evasion and dodge almost every attack. That seems like a good balance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387402#post1387402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not use the core book stat block. They're going to face a large pack of claw striders breed by an NPC in the past to be even nastier, that can operate as a Size 3 Elite Drill BG with higher baseline stats on top of it, with a non-QC &quot;alpha&quot; strider that can give orders to the pack, and 2-3 striders looking to be the next alpha, and all of them have increased stats as well. Just like if my group's PC are tearing apart militia stack block mortal troops, my answer doesn't have to be tossing in more and more and more militia troops when I can pick more potent troops, use BGs and commanders, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Size 3 battlegroup represents over 100 claw striders. That's a hell of a lot of dinosaurs. Not to say it couldn't exist in Creation, maybe you're attacking a long forgotten jungle city where everyone owns an ultra-claw strider as a pet and they all form together to defend the city or something, but that's gotta be a pretty rare occasion.<br /> <br /> That kind of arms race also might make your players feel like their heavily invested combat characters aren't actually that badass though. I don't want the Oblivion issue where Marauders end up wearing Daedric armor just to keep up with the player and continue to fullfill their role as random combat encounters. You built a character who can wrestle a Tyrant Lizard and throw him to the horizon, I don't want to just start putting in Uber Tyrant Lizards who then can't be wrestled or thrown to the horizon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387402#post1387402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're talking about a combat heavy Solar group... this is pretty damned hard to do even if they get enough initiative to threaten it. It just means the PCs are going to toss a motes in defense that they wouldn't against withering attacks or low damage decisive attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant kill the NPCs. Like &quot;Oh shit, this enemy has 12 initiative after that last attack, I go first with 30i though, so I'm just going to end him before he can use it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387402#post1387402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering having things like Glorious Solar Plate or Aegis of Invincible Might are there for Resistance Solars to grab? I'd say they have better Hardness options that makes DoOM's Hardness less and less appealing as time goes by.<br /> <br /> It's not just, &quot;as long as enemies are still using low initiative attacks,&quot; but also, &quot;as long as you never buy anything that can get you significantly better boosts too.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just how Hardness works, it doesn't stack so if you get a better source of it, you don't need the previous source. If you're not a resistance supernal, or just don't want to invest in those charms, you can still at least grab the 6 hardness from DOoM. Those charms have some of their own issues that make Durability of Oak not useless though. If you don't have time to activate Solar Plate, or don't feel like wearing golden plate armor where you are, or if you don't feel like spending 8+ offensive motes every round after activating the 8m Adamant Skin Technique and suffering your -3 penalty for at least two turns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387402#post1387402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the game itself is still a factor in this. If the game forces us to have characters act in a specific - frequently uncharacteristic - way just to make low Hardness feel useful... we're allowed to say the system is the problem. Otherwise what's the point of the system exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>What's uncharacteristic about a pack hunter going in for a kill and tearing off a piece? Remember, initiative is not an in-character resource. Every strike that a claw strider makes is meant to kill. Initiative can represent characters intentionally trying to put their foes off balance, but it usually doesn't. If my character goes for a withering thrust against your exposed face, he's trying to kill you, the difference between you blocking the attack, or getting hit by it is if you bat my blade away easily and keep focus, or if you just barely manage to turn it aside and shakily try to get your guard back up.<br /> <br /> When a claw strider goes for a low initiative attack, that is me dictating that it is narratively appropriate for one of these predators to dart in on this ambush and get the chance to wound somebody right off the hop. I do this all the time, in fact I did it in the last combat I ran with my friends, and the swordsman ended up in his -2s by the end of one quick fight due to a little bit of luck on the dice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387402#post1387402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, I find myself repeating that I'm not saying low damage decisive attacks should never happen. I'm saying they shouldn't be the required way lower tier enemies operate to matter, and once you cut out that mentality... it's a much rarer circumstance even if it will still happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it certainly helps lower tier enemies have a lasting impact. Low Hardness values don't really help against really powerful enemies as much, although they still can. A Solar using Invincible Fury of the Dawn to make five 5L attacks against you with only 10i gets a hard no-sell against Hardness 5. It's not very common though. On the other hand your Guile and Resolve of 3 are not especially helpful when the Socialize Supernal Eclipse cast sits your character down for a conversation, I don't think anyone expects them to be. Your guile of 3 is there so that you aren't an open book to anyone that takes a passing glance in your direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387402#post1387402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not asking what the point of Hardness 4 for a tick is when you can have Hardness 6 for a day. I'm asking if a character is trying to make Hardness a major part of their character's tactics, why are they stopping at low Hardness?<br /> <br /> To which the answer is, &quot;They shouldn't be.&quot; There's nothing wrong with jumping for better Hardness options just like any other thing your character might make a big part of your character's aptitudes, even if one official option among many others is particularly powerful/cheap.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if you're not making Hardness a major focal point of your character, but you want a little bit of it to give you some protection? Your Twilight anima isn't going to protect you from Octavian's massive 18i hit, but it's good enough to block yourself from being torn to shreds by Dragonblooded animas, and that happens fast. Especially since the Fire, Earth and Wood ones all have pretty devastating secondary effects which all trigger even if they're just dealing withering with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T22:10:49-07:00","id":1387413,"title":"","content":"I'm going to expand real quick here.<br /> <br /> RPGs are cool because they're fusion of roleplaying storytelling and a game. We're not just sitting around telling cool stories where we can do whatever we want, we can attempt whatever we want, but the rules are there to tell us when it is appropriate for something to succeed. We have a difficulty 3 lock to pick, the legendary super thief picks that almost every time, with his dicepool that he's modeled his character around, it is appropriate that he only fails that task like 5% of the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Combat and initiative is done the same way, it's just a bit weird because unlike a lot of other games where it just says &quot;How often is it appropriate for a character who's this physically strong to strike somebody that skilled in combat, and how much damage is it appropriate to deal?&quot; Exalted says &quot;When is it <i>narratively </i>appropriate for this attack to deal enough damage to slay a wounded opponent.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can roll Join Battle with my little dinosaurs, and decide that I want one of them to deal a real physical wound, but their initiative says that it is not, at this moment, narratively appropriate for them to be able to straight up kill an unwounded important character. It is only narratively appropriate if they deal a non-mortal wound or two in the initial ambush. Whereas Octavian who's spent the last two rounds beating the crap out of my exhausted DBs, and now has 30i, after such epic clashing and the characters just barely managing to keep his staff from crushing their skulls in, it is now narratively appropriate for Octavians hit to turn one of them into paste.<br /> <br /> The Hardness value that you get simply means that as long as you yourself are not crashed, it is never narratively appropriate to deal such a small wound. Any hit that actually drives metal deep into your body is going to be one that somebody had to work for at least a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T00:38:20-07:00","id":1387430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387410#post1387410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The claw striders might not know the difference between magical armor and mundane armor, armor is armor, but their attacks against the guy who's armor would no-sell them with its artifact awesomeness more often end up as withering attacks, and the ones against guys who's armor doesn't magically protect them so well end up getting cut.</div> </div> </div> </div>You specifically brought up the striders changing their in-character tactics to gang up on a crashed character that lost their Hardness, not just which type of attack they might use in the moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but that's gotta be a pretty rare occasion. </div> </div> </div>Well, fortunately that's far from the only trick the game allows you, because the game doesn't force me to just use claw striders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That kind of arms race also might make your players feel like their heavily invested combat characters aren't actually that badass though. </div> </div> </div>A certain amount of arms race is necessary to keep conflicts interesting as PCs get more powerful. RPGs have been doing this since, literally, the start of them.<br /> <br /> But, fortunately again, having the PCs run into uber-claw striders in their quest into a secret jungle ruin doesn't mean that the bandits they defeated earlier and try to ambush the PCs on the way back suddenly have massively improved gear/stats. The PCs get to slaughter them or show them mercy as they please because they've grown more powerful than before, and even after the efforts of their mission, can whoop those bandits easily. No video game style autoleveling of enemies.<br /> <br /> While 3e certainly needs the ST advice that Crucible of Legends is promised to be, for the sake of this conversation, can you not shift the goal posts with, &quot;OK, but what if bad STing follows your reasonable answer to my question?&quot; I never said, &quot;and then the whole world gets better starts,&quot; or, &quot;I'm house ruling in an Ultra Legendary Size,&quot; Merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's just how Hardness works,... </div> </div> </div>Which is... part of the problem with the utility of low Hardness, isn't it?<br /> <br /> While this can be partially addressed as Solar Resistance does via increasing it with later Charms, it seems pretty representative of the problem rather than a counterpoint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Those charms have some of their own issues that make Durability of Oak not useless though. </div> </div> </div>What did I say again?<br /> <br /> &quot;...less and less appealing as time goes by.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not, &quot;becomes useless.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's uncharacteristic about a pack hunter going in for a kill and tearing off a piece? </div> </div> </div>The part where they try to ambush their prey, it doesn't work, and they stick around to fight. Predators on the hunt don't stick around to fight to the death if their prey turns out to be tougher than expected. They go find something easier to kill and eat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember, initiative is not an in-character resource. </div> </div> </div>Gee, I love getting lectured on the basics of the game over something I didn't say. Don't you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not very common though. </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's the point exactly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the other hand your Guile and Resolve of 3 are not especially helpful when the Socialize Supernal Eclipse cast sits your character down for a conversation, I don't think anyone expects them to be. </div> </div> </div>Your 3s there aren't representing your supernatural prowess. Hardness is there to represent a part of that (or at least above human toughness for non-human base creatures with it). Which is a rather significant difference in how people are going to feel about them in play. You might not have the expectation that low level magical toughness is going to stop a supernatural murder machine from killing you, but you might reasonably have the expectation that might keep you alive a bit longer than if you didn't have it; and maybe enough for help to get to you and save you.<br /> <br /> Having some of the Guile boosting Charms might not stop a Socialize Supernal Eclipse powerhouse from reading my intentions, but it will at least make them work a bit harder for it than if I just sat there with my base Guile.<br /> <br /> Hardness doesn't accomplish that feeling. It does do stuff, but from a subjective experience level, it can be frustrating because of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if you're not making Hardness a major focal point of your character, but you want a little bit of it to give you some protection? </div> </div> </div>Then... you'd reasonably go for lower Hardness options for their lower buy-in and/or less complications. I'm not sure what you think I have all these positions I'm not saying or arguing. Did you really think this wasn't my position?<br /> <br /> I literally made the case that Hardness is one of the easiest things to grab a little of because of all the ways to get it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387413#post1387413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RPGs are cool because they're fusion of roleplaying storytelling and a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>... seriously?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Exalted says &quot;When is it <i>narratively </i>appropriate for this attack to deal enough damage to slay a wounded opponent.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Not really. Exalted isn't a narrative focused system, it's an emulation focused system. The combat system, and initiative in particular, isn't about establishing when it's narratively appropriate for an attack to deal enough damage to kill. It's about emulating big action set pieces where the characters attack a lot with little significant damage done, until a character thinks they're in a good spot to land a major hit; which might clinch a victory or fail and create a potential for a reversal of fortune. It was literally adapted from a fighting video-game... which is a narrative-less game design space.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Hardness value that you get simply means that as long as you yourself are not crashed, it is never narratively appropriate to deal such a small wound. Any hit that actually drives metal deep into your body is going to be one that somebody had to work for at least a little. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I do know how Hardness works mechanically... was that unclear at any point?<br /> <br /> I don't agree with the narrative part of this, but it's largely meaningless as a distinction for how useful low Hardness is.<br /> <br /> If you just want to pontificate on these things, I can shut up. But if you actually care about trying to engage with what I'm trying to communicate lets... focus on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T00:46:31-07:00","id":1387431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387413#post1387413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to expand real quick here.<br /> <br /> RPGs are cool because they're fusion of roleplaying storytelling and a game. We're not just sitting around telling cool stories where we can do whatever we want, we can attempt whatever we want, but the rules are there to tell us when it is appropriate for something to succeed. We have a difficulty 3 lock to pick, the legendary super thief picks that almost every time, with his dicepool that he's modeled his character around, it is appropriate that he only fails that task like 5% of the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Combat and initiative is done the same way, it's just a bit weird because unlike a lot of other games where it just says &quot;How often is it appropriate for a character who's this physically strong to strike somebody that skilled in combat, and how much damage is it appropriate to deal?&quot; Exalted says &quot;When is it <i>narratively </i>appropriate for this attack to deal enough damage to slay a wounded opponent.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can roll Join Battle with my little dinosaurs, and decide that I want one of them to deal a real physical wound, but their initiative says that it is not, at this moment, narratively appropriate for them to be able to straight up kill an unwounded important character. It is only narratively appropriate if they deal a non-mortal wound or two in the initial ambush. Whereas Octavian who's spent the last two rounds beating the crap out of my exhausted DBs, and now has 30i, after such epic clashing and the characters just barely managing to keep his staff from crushing their skulls in, it is now narratively appropriate for Octavians hit to turn one of them into paste.<br /> <br /> The Hardness value that you get simply means that as long as you yourself are not crashed, it is never narratively appropriate to deal such a small wound. Any hit that actually drives metal deep into your body is going to be one that somebody had to work for at least a little.</div> </div> </div> </div>Discussing that, I think there is actually a point I never thought of :<br /> <br /> When I think of the kind of scenes you are discussing, there are 2 kinds that come into my mind : The ones where the big badass protagonist/newly revealed enemy for the upcoming tournament arc take on a full attack from what seems an &quot;established&quot; character, and they are like &quot;What is this even ?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which then devolves into one of the 2 following cases :<br /> 1) It was nothing and he beats the crap out of the opponent he had<br /> 2) It was nothing on the spot and he beats the crap out of the opponents he had, but it's actually revealed that it was still a bit of something later. We've all seen this : The bad guy has actually a cut he didn't notice that was inflicted in the attack made by the protagonist (to show audience he might have a chance to be beaten with further training), or the protagonist explains later that he's actually a bit exhausted because the hit he took earlier took on a part of his strength.<br /> <br /> I'm one of the people that are not really a fan on how Hardness is implemented, but I know I can't totally change it because I'd have to rewrite everything and I don't have the skills of a developper. However, I'd be curious to see if someone has some suggestions on how to still impact the Hardness guy in a narrative impactful way, when the blow would be totally nullified by Hardness. Ideally, I would want it to : Have some kind of narrative impact (so it's not just &quot;you take a part of the damage&quot;), easy to do (not more than 1 roll, ideally no roll at all), and goes with the flow of combat (doesn't subtract Initiative or give malus to attack rolls because it makes things slower going on).<br /> <br /> Any ideas ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 05-11-2020, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T07:41:18-07:00","id":1387488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387430#post1387430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You specifically brought up the striders changing their in-character tactics to gang up on a crashed character that lost their Hardness, not just which type of attack they might use in the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are my out of character tactics using the striders to create drama. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387430#post1387430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While 3e certainly needs the ST advice that Crucible of Legends is promised to be, for the sake of this conversation, can you not shift the goal posts with, &quot;OK, but what if bad STing follows your reasonable answer to my question?&quot; I never said, &quot;and then the whole world gets better starts,&quot; or, &quot;I'm house ruling in an Ultra Legendary Size,&quot; Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay so what do you do for the 90% of times when you don't enhance what the antagonists statblocks put out?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387430#post1387430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is... part of the problem with the utility of low Hardness, isn't it?<br /> <br /> While this can be partially addressed as Solar Resistance does via increasing it with later Charms, it seems pretty representative of the problem rather than a counterpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why weak effects meant to counter weak opponents should be likewise strong against powerful opponents. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387430#post1387430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part where they try to ambush their prey, it doesn't work, and they stick around to fight. Predators on the hunt don't stick around to fight to the death if their prey turns out to be tougher than expected. They go find something easier to kill and eat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's why they launch a flurry of decisive attacks right off the bat and then when their fellows all get slaughtered by the Solars the last ones just book it, or die.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387430#post1387430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then... you'd reasonably go for lower Hardness options for their lower buy-in and/or less complications. I'm not sure what you think I have all these positions I'm not saying or arguing. Did you really think this wasn't my position?<br /> <br /> I literally made the case that Hardness is one of the easiest things to grab a little of because of all the ways to get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, yes if you want a little bit of Hardness you go for those options, and then use them when appropriate. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387430#post1387430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. Exalted isn't a narrative focused system, it's an emulation focused system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand the difference. The heading &quot;Withering Attacks and Drama&quot; says &quot;Withering attacks must be described as serious combat maneuvers-they're usually intended as killing or disabling blows by the characters who make them.&quot; so the characters themselves are not exclusively using withering attacks to maneuver into a position where they can kill their opponent, a lot of the time that big withering hammer strike at the start of combat is meant to cave their opponent's skull in.<br /> <br /> If we're saying there's some difference between emulation combat and narrative combat, why can't I say that I want my claw striders to emulate launching an ambush that results in some of the charaters taking bleeding wounds, but not die unless they're already wounded because that does not emulate epic fantasy combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T07:44:03-07:00","id":1387490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387431#post1387431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any ideas ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some charm effects have extra bonus damage that just ignores hardness, you could maybe use one of those. Also there's a lot of effects that you can apply just with a successful decisive attack, or even a withering one, like knock down, poison ect. Or even just a gambit.<br /> <br /> You might also just want to stunt the withering damage as leaving a significant, but not mechanically wounding scratch, which is something explicitly allowed if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T08:48:56-07:00","id":1387507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387431#post1387431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm one of the people that are not really a fan on how Hardness is implemented, but I know I can't totally change it because I'd have to rewrite everything and I don't have the skills of a developper. However, I'd be curious to see if someone has some suggestions on how to still impact the Hardness guy in a narrative impactful way, when the blow would be totally nullified by Hardness. Ideally, I would want it to : Have some kind of narrative impact (so it's not just &quot;you take a part of the damage&quot;), easy to do (not more than 1 roll, ideally no roll at all), and goes with the flow of combat (doesn't subtract Initiative or give malus to attack rolls because it makes things slower going on).<br /> <br /> Any ideas ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been clarified by the developers that poisoning someone only requires that the decisive attack hits, just make sure that you're clear on that before the attack roll takes place rather than let them assume that &quot;damage&quot; as a vector = tangible lost health levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T09:20:41-07:00","id":1387510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387507#post1387507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been clarified by the developers that poisoning someone only requires that the decisive attack hits, just make sure that you're clear on that before the attack roll takes place rather than let them assume that &quot;damage&quot; as a vector = tangible lost health levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not exactly what I'm looking for, even though poison could be a good idea. I don't really like poison in this game because there is no good reason not to use it.<br /> <br /> But that was not my point : I was more looking for an idea that made a decisive attack which has been soaked still &quot;interesting&quot;, besides the nullified damage. Poison is an interesting answer, but I'd like something a bit more &quot;universal&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T09:31:16-07:00","id":1387516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387510#post1387510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not exactly what I'm looking for, even though poison could be a good idea. I don't really like poison in this game because there is no good reason not to use it.<br /> <br /> But that was not my point : I was more looking for an idea that made a decisive attack which has been soaked still &amp;quot;interesting&amp;quot;, besides the nullified damage. Poison is an interesting answer, but I'd like something a bit more &amp;quot;universal&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean like, as a general rule whenever somebody tanks a full decisive hit with Hardness this bleed through effect will happen, or specifically when this Hardness effect triggers, or this particular attack triggers it still does something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T10:04:25-07:00","id":1387530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387510#post1387510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be curious to see if someone has some suggestions on how to still impact the Hardness guy in a narrative impactful way, when the blow would be totally nullified by Hardness. Ideally, I would want it to : Have some kind of narrative impact (so it's not just &quot;you take a part of the damage&quot;), easy to do (not more than 1 roll, ideally no roll at all), and goes with the flow of combat (doesn't subtract Initiative or give malus to attack rolls because it makes things slower going on).<br /> <br /> Any ideas ?</div> </div> </div> </div>-Negating a decisive with Hardness costs 1wp, if you can't (or won't) pay the hit goes through.<br /> <br /> -Same, but the cost increases by 1wp each time (so 1wp, then 2wp the next time, then 3wp, etc.) until you can't pay or you refuse to pay.<br /> <br /> -Negating a decisive with Hardness reduces your Hardness by (attacker's base initiative, normally 3). This is cumulative until a hit goes through at which point Hardness goes back to normal. This penalty can cause your Hardness to become negative, so it affects active Hardness as well as passive Hardness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T10:15:41-07:00","id":1387533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387530#post1387530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -Negating a decisive with Hardness costs 1wp, if you can't (or won't) pay the hit goes through.<br /> <br /> -Same, but the cost increases by 1wp each time (so 1wp, then 2wp the next time, then 3wp, etc.) until you can't pay or you refuse to pay.<br /> <br /> -Negating a decisive with Hardness reduces your Hardness by (attacker's base initiative, normally 3). This is cumulative until a hit goes through at which point Hardness goes back to normal. This penalty can cause your Hardness to become negative, so it affects active Hardness as well as passive Hardness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the first idea, even though it seems quite punitive, but I definitely like the idea.<br /> <br /> The last one seems good, but it might be a little too complex to track. Still, it ensure the fight will go forward in a simple manner because sooner or later it makes sure you will take a hit. I like it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> I mean as a general rule when somebody negates an attack with Hardness, some mechanical effect that still makes the &quot;fight goes forward&quot;. I'd like to have a clever Initiative rule that keep the fight on edge even though a Decisive attack just got cancelled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T10:43:07-07:00","id":1387541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387391#post1387391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because to me, it seems like you were asking what's the point of Hardness 4 when you could so easily just get Hardness 6 for a whole day for free. The answer is you should not so easily be able to get Hardness 6 for a whole day for free.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Disagree.<br /> <br /> ISoB is Obvious. It can be Distorted. It immediately pegs you as a Sorcerer. It makes you REALLY heavy. Even with Excellency it takes a couple of turns to cast.<br /> <br /> It probably shouldn't stack with armor (what with how it counts as Medium Armor and all). But it's not broken for the sake of day long Hardness.<br /> <br /> Considering the cost of a Spell vs the cost of buying Artifact armor... I think it's a pretty fair balance point. Charms have the advantage of subtly and building to higher powers on their tree. Plus they usually have other effects, DoOM is a great Essence 1 opening Charm (especially considering mote regeneration).<br /> <br /> Exalted isn't balanced. The balance comes from the ST. My character casts ISoB before breakfast every day, so my ST made me fight on a precarious ledge that wouldn't support my weight half a mile in the air.<br /> <br /> If you never fight enemy sorcerers, never need to fight in mud (or the second story of a building), never suffer social concequences from being a Sorcerer/being a Sorcerer is always appropriate for your character concept, you are not a Martial Artist, are never ambushed in your sleep AND never have to use Invincible God Metal Flash <i>and</i> you can't just wear Freedom's Cadence (or Silken Armor or Mela's Coil or a Warstrider) <i>then</i> sure ISoB is overpowered (unless you are a Deeb who had to spend 4 Charms as prereqs).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-11-2020, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T11:19:11-07:00","id":1387546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387510#post1387510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not exactly what I'm looking for, even though poison could be a good idea. I don't really like poison in this game because there is no good reason not to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW most weapons aren't poisonable as the tag appears almost exclusively on light thrown weapons. While not the most realistic way to handle it kind of makes sense in context of it's interaction with hardness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T12:00:13-07:00","id":1387561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387541#post1387541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. Disagree.<br /> <br /> ISoB is Obvious. It can be Distorted. It immediately pegs you as a Sorcerer. It makes you REALLY heavy. Even with Excellency it takes a couple of turns to cast.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm you may be right. My experience might be twisted by the fact that I used it in a west game and not once did any of the downsides show up, but at least twice I got to hold my breath and completely avoid a deadly contact poison. In retrospect the fact that I never was the object of mistrust for being a big solid bronze man, or never had to worry about sinking to the bottom of the ocean in a big sailing game was very lucky:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T12:55:18-07:00","id":1387574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387546#post1387546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RAW most weapons aren't poisonable as the tag appears almost exclusively on light thrown weapons. While not the most realistic way to handle it kind of makes sense in context of it's interaction with hardness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the time I've used poison, it was through MA charms. Serpent and Black Claw, obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T14:47:02-07:00","id":1387594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387546#post1387546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RAW most weapons aren't poisonable as the tag appears almost exclusively on light thrown weapons. While not the most realistic way to handle it kind of makes sense in context of it's interaction with hardness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eeeeeehhhhh... by that logic you can't use a sword whilst mounted.<br /> <br /> Given the presence of the One Handed tag in Archery, I choose to interpret Poisonable in Thrown to mean you can't poison a boomerang rather than you can't poison any weapon other than darts, needles and shuriken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1211052#post1211052\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1211052#post1211052\"> Ask the Devs - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1211052#post1211052\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1211052#post1211052 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Dear Exalted fans, as you may be aware from the latest Onyx Path Monday Meeting notes (http://theonyxpath.com/princes-gambit-joy-exalted-plans-monday-meeting-notes/), Robert Vance and I have been honored with the opportunity to take on line editor duties for Exalted Third Edition. As part of that, we want to make ourselves available to the community as a resource to keep you informed as best we can about the line. Obviously there will be some questions we can't answer! But when we're not working on upcoming books, we'll drop in to touch base. We'll be using this thread as our port of call so that we </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1215684#post1215684\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1215684#post1215684\"> Ask the Devs - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1215684#post1215684\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1215684#post1215684 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Dear Exalted fans, as you may be aware from the latest Onyx Path Monday Meeting notes (http://theonyxpath.com/princes-gambit-joy-exalted-plans-monday-meeting-notes/), Robert Vance and I have been honored with the opportunity to take on line editor duties for Exalted Third Edition. As part of that, we want to make ourselves available to the community as a resource to keep you informed as best we can about the line. Obviously there will be some questions we can't answer! But when we're not working on upcoming books, we'll drop in to touch base. We'll be using this thread as our port of call so that we </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-11-2020, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T15:37:43-07:00","id":1387608,"title":"","content":"There's not really a take on it that isn't dumb. You can't poison sling bullets or a boomerang but you can poison a chain or a hammer... okay then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T16:05:06-07:00","id":1387611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387431#post1387431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(doesn't subtract Initiative or give malus to attack rolls because it makes things slower going on).<br /> <br /> Any ideas ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kind of hard to add a drawback that doesn't slow things down in some sense.<br /> <br /> That said, maybe something like: After Hardness that persists longer than a turn is used to negate damage, on the next turn it cannot be applied unless the user makes a Misc. Action to reset it, otherwise it will return the turn after that.<br /> <br /> Basically, Hardness from longer duration sources would default to only working every other turn, or you'd have to flurry in a Misc. Action (and there might still be a window for someone to hit you before you go even if that's going to be a fairly uncommon set of circumstances where they'd need higher Init than you, and still have less than necessary to defeat your Hardness). However powers like DoOM and the Twilight Anima non-automatic version would allow you to have Hardness every turn at the cost of motes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387488#post1387488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are my out of character tactics using the striders to create drama.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, yeah, that was kind of my point? It's not the claw striders acting in a fashion driven by &quot;what would a claw strider do?&quot; it's ignoring what a claw strider would do (and not picking an enemy that might more naturally behave that way) and having them use tactics designed to add significant risk to the PCs engaging in fighting weaker foes with the understanding that they're going to be at risk from attrition in the scenario at hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay so what do you do for the 90% of times when you don't enhance what the antagonists statblocks put out? </div> </div> </div>I don't recall specifying any level of frequency.<br /> <br /> How I design foes for PCs is dependent on what my goal is. Not every fight the characters get in is going to even be combat, let alone challenging combat, just enough that the combat heavies (even if that's the whole group) feel like they're having their fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't see why weak effects meant to counter weak opponents should be likewise strong against powerful opponents. </div> </div> </div>Because... this is a strawman?<br /> <br /> Weak effects are meant to counter weak effects. Hardness 5 stops a 5i attack from a peasant dirt farmer nobody as well as it does from a Solar.<br /> <br /> Taking some low level Hardness because you foresee fighting a lot of Dragonblooded isn't because you're thinking of Dragonblooded as weak opponents.<br /> <br /> Despite my frustration with it, you already made the point here earlier: a Charm that's the same as a weaker Charm, but better in every way is bad design.<br /> <br /> If you want a better Excellent Strike Charm, you don't make Excellent Strike obsolete, you make an upgrade Charm, or something that's better but has major drawbacks (like resets, or harder to regain resources like WP, etc.).<br /> <br /> But that's basically how Hardness works. You don't upgrade weak Hardness to keep up with stronger attacks. You buy better Hardness and leave the weak Hardness behind. Even if Artifact light and heavy armor have reasonable trade offs side by side, as you add Charms, XP, get larger mote pools, etc. You can buy away the negatives of heavy armor, but you can't upgrade the light armor (outside of home brewed Evocations and such, but you could make super-heavy with the same thing, so I think it's reasonable to consider that a wash) to match. <br /> <br /> One of the things the lowers the utility of low Hardness values is that they become obsolete instead of getting built on; and frequently become made obsolete by relatively low level stuff. <br /> <br /> Again, not everyone is going to want to sink three or four Charms into making heavy armor's drawbacks go away, and they'll be fine with light's Hardness.<br /> <br /> But in the grand scheme of how useful Hardness is at different levels, this design reduces low Hardness usefulness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, that's why they launch a flurry of decisive attacks right off the bat and then when their fellows all get slaughtered by the Solars the last ones just book it, or die. </div> </div> </div>Or, really, when they notice they've been spotted (they're ambush predators, and 6 dice might work against a yeddim, but if that's enough to gank a group of Solar PCs... the Solars are probably in for a very rough time beyond the animal attacks), they wait for something less observant to pass by.<br /> <br /> If the claw striders are being attacked before they've even gotten to launch that flurry of decisive attacks... what are they sticking around for? I mean, your whole example is predicated on them failing to get in their ambush at the start of the fight; justifiably, but that ambush is their primary tactic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't understand the difference. </div> </div> </div>A narrative focused combat system is about resolving a fight based on the needs of the story. QCs wouldn't be stated up as condensed characters, but as a series of traits for the different roles in a fight. Narrative combat systems don't need to tell you the difference in accuracy and damage between two claw strider attacks, they need to tell the GM what kind of narratives they're meant to be good for, and then have a simple way to translate that into resolution. For example instead of bite and claw, they'd have a very impressive first round attack, a mediocre second round attack, and shitty third round or more attacks, to fulfill a roll of being their mostly to pose a risk of attrition in a short fight as part of the narrative of grinding down the party as they proceed through a dangerous trek.<br /> <br /> An emulation system is one focused on establishing a feel to how combat flows to create an aesthetic experience. Exalted 3e is already a good example of it. Instead of a WoD fight where characters are attacking each other as everyone gets weaker and weaker, and the winner is the one that can hold out the longest, Exalted 3e adds on the Initiative layer to emulate action set pieces better.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T18:08:05-07:00","id":1387625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387611#post1387611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in the grand scheme of how useful Hardness is at different levels, this design reduces low Hardness usefulness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, the bottom line is basically this. As a storyteller I use plenty of low initiative attacks at all levels of play. I find it does a good job of making otherwise not very threatening enemies matter more, it's good for finishing off enemies that are close to death, and just making combat a lot more meaningful and dramatic overall as players go through a series of scenes slowly accruing battle damage.<br /> <br /> I even use them as a player, especially when something like a big badass enemy is sitting at 30i and ready to one hit KO my circlemate, and then somebody launches a decisive to put him down...which ends up only putting him to his -4. Why is an enemy in their -4s still dangerous? Well maybe their dicepools are just that good, or maybe they have wound penalty ignoring charms, or maybe their last health level isn't even a -4. At that point I turn on Burning Fury Wreath to ignore their 5 Hardness and fire off my last attack to kick them down for good. Or even when they're not that dangerous but I just don't want to waste a huge damage attack inflicting the last 1-2 health levels I need.<br /> <br /> You might not think it works, but I use it, and it definitely works for me. In my games if you have a Twilight anima banner active, you will get use out of it even at high level, you don't need to upgrade to Hardness 10 when you get past Essence 3. Nevermind the fact that with Supernal and Solars you could well have an Essence 1 character who's twice as badass as an Essence 5 one anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387611#post1387611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, really, when they notice they've been spotted (they're ambush predators, and 6 dice might work against a yeddim, but if that's enough to gank a group of Solar PCs... the Solars are probably in for a very rough time beyond the animal attacks), they wait for something less observant to pass by.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well maybe they're starving and just going to go for it until some of them start dropping.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387611#post1387611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An emulation system is one focused on establishing a feel to how combat flows to create an aesthetic experience. Exalted 3e is already a good example of it. Instead of a WoD fight where characters are attacking each other as everyone gets weaker and weaker, and the winner is the one that can hold out the longest, Exalted 3e adds on the Initiative layer to emulate action set pieces better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay I was using the terms wrong. In an emulation style though I still don't have to match up what the character is wanting do to with what I'm wanting to do. The character is going for a killshot almost every time, that's their strategy. When they try to make a 4i decisive attack they are very legitimately attempting to kill their enemy, it just won't be lethal to a full health character because the fights that Ex3 is trying to emulate don't go down like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 05-11-2020, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T00:45:02-07:00","id":1387657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387611#post1387611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's kind of hard to add a drawback that doesn't slow things down in some sense.<br /> <br /> That said, maybe something like: After Hardness that persists longer than a turn is used to negate damage, on the next turn it cannot be applied unless the user makes a Misc. Action to reset it, otherwise it will return the turn after that.<br /> <br /> Basically, Hardness from longer duration sources would default to only working every other turn, or you'd have to flurry in a Misc. Action (and there might still be a window for someone to hit you before you go even if that's going to be a fairly uncommon set of circumstances where they'd need higher Init than you, and still have less than necessary to defeat your Hardness). However powers like DoOM and the Twilight Anima non-automatic version would allow you to have Hardness every turn at the cost of motes.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think I like Epitome's proposition to reduce Hardness from the Initiative Damage Pool you would have taken. No dices involved, the player just mark the malus, and it still makes the fight going forward because it means you will take damage later on. <br /> <br /> Not to combine with idiotic 5 useless PNJ who spam Decisive Attacks but I'm not this kind of ST so this should be good with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T09:41:45-07:00","id":1387745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387611#post1387611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weak effects are meant to counter weak effects. Hardness 5 stops a 5i attack from a peasant dirt farmer nobody as well as it does from a Solar.<br /> <br /> Taking some low level Hardness because you foresee fighting a lot of Dragonblooded isn't because you're thinking of Dragonblooded as weak opponents.<br /> <br /> Despite my frustration with it, you already made the point here earlier: a Charm that's the same as a weaker Charm, but better in every way is bad design.<br /> <br /> If you want a better Excellent Strike Charm, you don't make Excellent Strike obsolete, you make an upgrade Charm, or something that's better but has major drawbacks (like resets, or harder to regain resources like WP, etc.).<br /> <br /> But that's basically how Hardness works. <b>You don't upgrade weak Hardness to keep up with stronger attacks.</b> You buy better Hardness and leave the weak Hardness behind. Even if Artifact light and heavy armor have reasonable trade offs side by side, as you add Charms, XP, get larger mote pools, etc. You can buy away the negatives of heavy armor, but you can't upgrade the light armor (outside of home brewed Evocations and such, but you could make super-heavy with the same thing, so I think it's reasonable to consider that a wash) to match. <br /> <br /> One of the things the lowers the utility of low Hardness values is that they become obsolete instead of getting built on; and frequently become made obsolete by relatively low level stuff. <br /> <br /> Again, not everyone is going to want to sink three or four Charms into making heavy armor's drawbacks go away, and they'll be fine with light's Hardness.<br /> <br /> But in the grand scheme of how useful Hardness is at different levels, this design reduces low Hardness usefulness.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something I feel I can productively engage with.<br /> <br /> I don't think this is true.<br /> <br /> Yes, if you wear Heavy Artifact Armor with Armored Scouts Invigoration then the Hardness 10 trumps the Hardness 4 of DoOM. But you can still use DoOM against Withering attacks. And you can still use DoOM' s Decisive damage reduction to add 2 pseudo-Hardness. Diamond Body Prana doesn't stack with any armor, but you can still use it to get Hardness when you are not wearing armor. And it stacks with/upgrades DoOM. <br /> <br /> If you were already using Light Artifact Armor, then Armored Scott's Invigoration gives a bonus instead of removing a penalty (so you CAN improve Light armor, even with canon Charms). If using Medium then it's cheaper than using Heavy.<br /> <br /> Invulnerable Skin of Bronze has numerous drawbacks that DoOM doesn't have. And yes, I'll give you Hardness doesn't stack but the Soak will stack with your Artifact Armor and the Hardness will stack with DoOM.<br /> <br /> I don't think there are any Solar effects that give Hardness which you will never use once you get a better source of Hardness. I'm not familiar enough with Lunars to comment, but it's not a problem I have personally had with Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> I get the <i>perception</i> (&quot;I have Hardness 10. An effect with gives Hardness 4 is useless!&quot;). I just don't get how this actually happens in actual play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T13:08:29-07:00","id":1387791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387625#post1387625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might not think it works, but I use it, and it definitely works for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying that it &quot;doesn't work.&quot; I'm saying, &quot;DrLoveMonkey's personal style,&quot; doesn't automatically counter the reasons expressed for why Hardness at low value is either practically or aesthetically less useful than it seems like it should be.<br /> <br /> Telling people to run games more like someone else isn't really a satisfactory answer to a lot of people either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387657#post1387657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I like Epitome's proposition to reduce Hardness from the Initiative Damage Pool you would have taken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, just offering a different option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387745#post1387745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you can still use DoOM against Withering attacks. And you can still use DoOM' s Decisive damage reduction to add 2 pseudo-Hardness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, as well acknowledged already up-thread, DoOM remains a useful Charm because of the damage reduce part of it, even if the Hardness part doesn't (it's also useful in upper level combat if the &quot;ignore Hardness&quot; effects start to get broken out).<br /> <br /> But the question isn't &quot;is DoOM a decent Charm even if you have better sources of Hardness,&quot; but, &quot;are lower levels of Hardness really that useful?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you were already using Light Artifact Armor, then Armored Scott's Invigoration gives a bonus instead of removing a penalty (so you CAN improve Light armor, even with canon Charms). If using Medium then it's cheaper than using Heavy. </div> </div> </div>ASI's bonus isn't to light isn't to armor stats. Frankly, it's a waste of 4m unless you have zero Awareness or other JB enhancing Charms (which you could have bought instead of ASI). 4m for an indefinite re-roll one failed JB die isn't anything to write home about.<br /> <br /> And if you're, say, using Glorious Solar Plate, ASI activates for free when you turn it on. And with how 3e handles the 'item out of glowy light Charms,' you're not even cutting yourself off from Evocations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I get the <i>perception</i> (&quot;I have Hardness 10. An effect with gives Hardness 4 is useless!&quot;). I just don't get how this actually happens in actual play. </div> </div> </div>Easily. Because it's not about if Hardness granting effects become useless even if the Hardness aspect of them does. DoOM, ISoB, etc. remain useful because the do more than grant you Hardness, even if the Hardness they also grant you is something you never end up using. It's about the fact that you're not using them for Hardness.<br /> <br /> Or, to put it another way, if DoOM was a Uniform Charm, with just the reduction aspect, and Diamond Body Prana granted the same Hardness as it does in combo with DoOM RAW, I don't think anyone would complain or even notice. Diamond Body Prana would just be the &quot;I want to go unarmored route,&quot; Charm, and people that want to use armor would pick up that part of the tree instead. Everyone would still be taking DoOM because damage reduction like that at Essence 1 is really useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T14:12:38-07:00","id":1387806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387791#post1387791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not saying that it &quot;doesn't work.&quot; I'm saying, &quot;DrLoveMonkey's personal style,&quot; doesn't automatically counter the reasons expressed for why Hardness at low value is either practically or aesthetically less useful than it seems like it should be.<br /> <br /> Telling people to run games more like someone else isn't really a satisfactory answer to a lot of people either.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't think a game element is fun, there are two options:<br /> <br /> 1. The game is wrong. Houserule a change to fix this.<br /> 2. You are playing wrong. Change your playstyle to fix this.<br /> <br /> The Doctor and I enjoy Hardness. If you played more like us, I think you'd like it too. If you'd rather houserule a change, I'm sure the community could help with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, as well acknowledged already up-thread, DoOM remains a useful Charm because of the damage reduce part of it, even if the Hardness part doesn't (it's also useful in upper level combat if the &quot;ignore Hardness&quot; effects start to get broken out).<br /> <br /> But the question isn't &quot;is DoOM a decent Charm even if you have better sources of Hardness,&quot; but, &quot;are lower levels of Hardness really that useful?&quot; </div> </div> </div>Yes. For the reasons also enumerated upthread, low levels of Hardness are useful.<br /> <br /> The ultilty of low level Hardness is going to depend on playstyle. This is true for literally every game element.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Easily. Because it's not about if Hardness granting effects become useless even if the Hardness aspect of them does. DoOM, ISoB, etc. remain useful because the do more than grant you Hardness, even if the Hardness they also grant you is something you never end up using. It's about the fact that you're not using them for Hardness.<br /> <br /> Or, to put it another way, if DoOM was a Uniform Charm, with just the reduction aspect, and Diamond Body Prana granted the same Hardness as it does in combo with DoOM RAW, I don't think anyone would complain or even notice. Diamond Body Prana would just be the &quot;I want to go unarmored route,&quot; Charm, and people that want to use armor would pick up that part of the tree instead. Everyone would still be taking DoOM because damage reduction like that at Essence 1 is really useful. </div> </div> </div>I think people whose characters wear non-artifact armor would notice.<br /> <br /> I also think the current design is great game balance. If you don't have Hardness, DoOM gives you Hardness. If you do have Hardness DoOM is still useful. Same for ISoB.<br /> <br /> Low levels of Hardness stop weak attacks.<br /> You literally cannot get low levels of Hardness unless it's attached to an effect that's still useful even if the Hardness isn't.<br /> The uses of Solar Hardness may be niche (only when Crashed, only when caught out of armor, only when I summon armor made of golden light, only when I spend time to cast an Obvious spell, only when wearing conspicuous magic armor (with a mobility penalty)) but they're never useless.<br /> <br /> Even if you have Heavy Artifact Armor, DoOM is still useful <i>for Hardness</i> if you are attacked outside of your armor. AND the Charm is still useful whilst wearing armor, even if the Hardness isn't.<br /> <br /> I don't expect this answer will be satisfactory to you, but all I can suggest is that you houserule something different. Maybe say all sources of Hardness are always Hardness 10, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-14-2020, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T15:15:43-07:00","id":1387817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387806#post1387806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't think a game element is fun, there are two options:</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem far too intent to make everything a binary when it's not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. The game is wrong. Houserule a change to fix this.<br /> 2. You are playing wrong. Change your playstyle to fix this. </div> </div> </div>There's actually a third option: play the game anyway. Hardness isn't some lynchpin of the system where the game falls apart without it. I've played a 3e heroic mortals game... which makes Hardness something basically nobody has (not impossible because mortals can still access sorcery, but in that game we were asked not to make sorcerers). It was fun.<br /> <br /> For our Solar games, pretty much all of the Hardness granting powers are part of packages that are useful even if the Hardness part isn't really that useful because you can get better elsewhere.<br /> <br /> The lack of lasting utility to low Hardness levels is unfun, but also avoidable enough that it's easier to move on and play than doing extensive house rules or trying to change our playstyles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you played more like us, I think you'd like it too. If you'd rather houserule a change, I'm sure the community could help with that. </div> </div> </div>My dislike of how Hardness is implemented goes beyond the scope of this thread (which I've pointed to before this), so I highly doubt I would be happy with it just because more low damage decisive attacks were being thrown around. I can assure you that for myself, I would find taking a low Hardness power just to avoid dealing with my ST's focus on attrition combat encounters exceedingly grating. I don't play Exalted to get my long term resource management survival kick (there are plenty of games that do that well, which I enjoy playing). I play Exalted to play epic heroes<br /> <br /> This is not the first thread in which I've brought up my discontent with Hardness; haven't really gotten much help in the past about that. I've gotten a lot of, &quot;Hardness is fine, just play different,&quot; in response though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes. For the reasons also enumerated upthread, low levels of Hardness are useful. </div> </div> </div>But the question isn't binary. How useful is it? Well, as you acknowledge, it's rather niche.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think people whose characters wear non-artifact armor would notice. </div> </div> </div>If you're wearing non-Artifact armor... GSP has an option for you. Since the prereqs for GSP are useful to armor of any type, if you're planning on playing a Solar that uses armor the investment to get to GSP's 10 Hardness isn't going to seem onerous. Or, other options that are out there.<br /> <br /> It also makes unarmored Resistance Solars and armored Resistance Solars have different styles (unarmored doesn't get as high, but has the reflexive stuff, armored trades that speed for better protection).<br /> <br /> Though it doesn't really feel like you're engaging much with the thought exercise posed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't expect this answer will be satisfactory to you,... </div> </div> </div>Because you refuse to actually engage with the premise of the discussion.<br /> <br /> Let's try something different:<br /> <br /> Is Lionesses assessment in post #31 accurate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T18:07:43-07:00","id":1387852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387791#post1387791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Telling people to run games more like someone else isn't really a satisfactory answer to a lot of people either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be fair here that isn't how I used to run Ex3. I used to think &quot;Okay, this guy has basically zero chance to kill the player with 6i, and he knows that, so he's not going to decisive.&quot; which ended up with a lot of people buying healing magics and wound penalty ignoring charms that were otherwise useless. Then eventually the one big enemy who was actually badass enough to get into a position of strength, and keep it long enough to hit with a decisive attack came around...and then he misses that attack anyway with bad luck. Or he hits, maybe deals some sizable damage, but then like an in-game week passes by without anything really critical happening, especially nothing risking dealing health level damage to the wounded PC, and we're back to square one.<br /> <br /> Since changing my strategy though, things have been running a lot better. I've been able to use more base enemies without having to pile on homebrew modifications to them, combat has more punch, there's really good reasons to take charms that otherwise wouldn't be useful, and my players have become a lot more thoughtful about the game.<br /> <br /> I'm not bending over backwards to try and make low Hardness work, I changed my game style based on the suggestions of some other people on the site and the whole combat game is better, and as a result also lower values of Hardness now are seeing more use. I also take the instances of low Hardness to be an indication that this is how the game is supposed to be run, along with the number of antagonists/charms that gain bonuses against enemies suffering from wound penalties, or who themselves gain bonuses by having wound penalties.<br /> <br /> <br /> Something else I've basically never used even now is cover. The Solar charm Angle-Tracing Edge would be 100% useless in every game of e3 that I've run so far. Also difficult terrain, I believe I may have used it at some point, but I can't quite remember. Now though I'm thinking &quot;Hey, what if I had some enemy archers up somewhere in cover, and the only way to get to them is through difficult terrain?&quot; that's a pretty smart tactic anyway and makes a lot of the lesser used charms better if that's an element of the game to boot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T23:47:41-07:00","id":1387935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387817#post1387817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You seem far too intent to make everything a binary when it's not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There's actually a third option: play the game anyway. Hardness isn't some lynchpin of the system where the game falls apart without it. I've played a 3e heroic mortals game... which makes Hardness something basically nobody has (not impossible because mortals can still access sorcery, but in that game we were asked not to make sorcerers). It was fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would suggest that if Hardness being unfun is a non-issue for you, then arguing about it for five pages is not a productive use of time. As ever, I am impressed with your grasp of rhetoric but bewildered by what you actually <i>want</i>.<br /> <br /> Are you just venting?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387817#post1387817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's try something different:<br /> <br /> Is Lionesses assessment in post #31 accurate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I think that's fair.<br /> <br /> I've built my entire 3E character around the Smashing tag -- he uses it on every attack in every combat (except maybe and handful of times when he was Crashed or threw javelins instead). I suppose one could do the same with Hardness. My character also has the Reaching tag -- never used it once. I suppose the same could be true of Hardness. My character also has Hardness 8 and the Two-handed tag, comes up every other session or so -- when I was forced to fight without Hardness, I really noticed the difference, just as being Grappled is an immediate game-changer for my character.<br /> <br /> Do you agree that low levels of Hardness have utility comparable to a weapon tag?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-14-2020, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T02:41:17-07:00","id":1387965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387852#post1387852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used to think &quot;Okay, this guy has basically zero chance to kill the player with 6i, and he knows that, so he's not going to decisive.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>For my group, the decisive decision is, well, if the decisive has a chance to significantly alter the stakes/situation/outcome of the battle 6i decisive attacks happen, they just usually mean a gambit rather than a damaging attack is being attempted. 6i is plenty to establish a grapple, or use a Disarming weapon to disarm.<br /> <br /> It just didn't really help improve my impression of low Hardness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Something else I've basically never used even now is cover. The Solar charm Angle-Tracing Edge would be 100% useless in every game of e3 that I've run so far. Also difficult terrain, I believe I may have used it at some point, but I can't quite remember. Now though I'm thinking &quot;Hey, what if I had some enemy archers up somewhere in cover, and the only way to get to them is through difficult terrain?&quot; that's a pretty smart tactic anyway and makes a lot of the lesser used charms better if that's an element of the game to boot. </div> </div> </div>And... cover and rough terrain come up in my first 3e fight (and Reach for JonDoe's examples), because our ST decided to use mounted enemies figuring it would give them a bit of a boost against a bunch of Solars. Which it did until my character uses some Athletics Charms to boost his efforts to knock down a bunch of trees to rough up the terrain against their melee fighters, and give our ranged fighters some cover.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure what point this makes... but perhaps not all of this is really just play style.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387935#post1387935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would suggest that if Hardness being unfun is a non-issue for you, then arguing about it for five pages is not a productive use of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said it was a non-issue, I said it was an issue I can get past and still enjoy playing the game with my friends. I've never played an RPG that didn't have some mechanic somewhere that annoyed me, but a lot of the people I play with aren't up for a lot of house-rules and tinkering. So generally I save my advocacy for changes for rules that would negatively impact me a lot more than stuff I can easily just avoid by not taking it.<br /> <br /> As for the productivity? Why aren't use asking DrLoveMonkey the same question? Or is that a question that only matters if someone holds a different position than your own?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As ever, I am impressed with your grasp of rhetoric but bewildered by what you actually <i>want</i>. </div> </div> </div>To actually discuss the topic of the thread. I have my opinions about it, you have your opinions about it, they differ... so I'd like to see if there's a reason beyond play style to actually consider here.<br /> <br /> But even when it seems like when it seems like there's actually more to agree on that it seems, it's like pulling teeth to get there.<br /> <br /> It's like trying to debate against a Rule Zero Fallacy with someone that refuses to acknowledge that's what they're doing. You come off as so far into &quot;here's how we make low Hardness matter more,&quot; mindset that you don't realize that you're also coming off as arguing that low Hardness needs to be lifted up; whether by changes to style, rules or whatever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are you just venting? </div> </div> </div>Do you realize that this sort of questioning of my motives negatively impacts the way more innocent intended questions are intended to be taken?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, I think that's fair. </div> </div> </div>OK. We both agree that low Hardness is, by itself, a niche effect that's generally only taken as part of a pack of effects; and thus the answer to the general question of the thread is, &quot;not very, but you'll probably have it from one of those packages, and when it is useful hey, you'll have it.&quot;<br /> <br /> We don't need to debate about how good DoOM is, or if Solar sorcerers perhaps get a bit too much for the investment, or any of that? Most of the last 4 pages really?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you agree that low levels of Hardness have utility comparable to a weapon tag? </div> </div> </div>In a very broad sense, as I consider the weapon tags an ugly mess of mixed utility.<br /> <br /> But this gets back to an earlier point: the subjective &quot;fun&quot; factor. Weapons are, generally speaking, free. Yes, they have a Resources cost attached to them, but there's lots of ways to get weapons even without money. A weapon with a tag that you never end up using didn't effectively cost you anything. Chopping is probably one of the lowest utility/most niche weapon tags due to the cost of use relative to benefits gained, it's not like you're paying extra just to have it.<br /> <br /> Hardness, as a supernatural/superhuman effect, has a cost to it. All the cool packages that include it seem safe to assume would be cheaper if they didn't include Hardness.<br /> <br /> As a hypothetical thought experiment, imagine players could pick between two different versions of DoOM. One RAW, and the other without the Hardness attached. As Charms the cost the buy them is inherently the same. So, the second version of DoOM, as it gives less, should still cost less, right? It would be fair to say, cost 1m less to activate? <br /> <br /> Because that's part of the issue beyond agreeing that low Hardness is already a relatively niche effect that most people only have because it's part of a bigger package. I can't buy my hypothetical no-Hardness DoOM where I can get the part I'd use a lot, without the part I barely if ever use, and save 1m per use. I've got to take the package deal.<br /> <br /> So I feel like I should be getting something for what I'm paying for. Isn't that a fair feeling to have about this?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:49:49-07:00","id":1388027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387745#post1387745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something I feel I can productively engage with.<br /> <br /> I don't think this is true.<br /> <br /> Yes, if you wear Heavy Artifact Armor with Armored Scouts Invigoration then the Hardness 10 trumps the Hardness 4 of DoOM. But you can still use DoOM against Withering attacks. And you can still use DoOM' s Decisive damage reduction to add 2 pseudo-Hardness. Diamond Body Prana doesn't stack with any armor, but you can still use it to get Hardness when you are not wearing armor. And it stacks with/upgrades DoOM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Complementary to this, it's important to remember <i>how</i> you receive decisive attacks. And, again, the fact that hardness comes in a package.<br /> <br /> Outside enhanced multiattacks, the enemy usually <i>has</i> to build initiative up. This is expensive, and won't always ignore hardness.<br /> If you have, say, hardness 10, a pretty Invincible Fury Of The Dawn + Fire &amp; Stones Strike with perfect hit thresholds will need to have anywhere from 14 to 35 initiative to deal damage. The former is much easier to get but you're paying 8m 1wp for 8 dice of damage (more if you account for the probable excellent strike to make that hit threshold safer). And a single DoOM activation whiffs all of them if the assailant doesn't build another 4 to 10 initiative. <br /> <br /> Back to more standard applications, the attacker needs to build more initiative than the defender's hardness to deal decisive damage.<br /> <br /> Let's look at the habitual 4-10 hardness range.<br /> <br /> Consider Eevil Kneevil is at 9i and withered you for a nice 18 raw damage attack. If you have 8 soak, he likely upped to 15i. If you have 15 soak, he likely went to 12i. <br /> If you had low soak, you will deny him a decisive against your hardness if you deal 5 to 11 damage. If you had high soak, you will deny him by dealing 2-8 damage.<br /> <br /> Hardness means the enemy doesn't want to Thousand-Cuts you, and can't gamble into a death spiral. Damage and Soak are how you <b>force</b> the enemy into that scenario.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T09:59:38-07:00","id":1388075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387965#post1387965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... cover and rough terrain come up in my first 3e fight (and Reach for JonDoe's examples), because our ST decided to use mounted enemies figuring it would give them a bit of a boost against a bunch of Solars. Which it did until my character uses some Athletics Charms to boost his efforts to knock down a bunch of trees to rough up the terrain against their melee fighters, and give our ranged fighters some cover.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure what point this makes... but perhaps not all of this is really just play style.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it shows it IS about playstyle. What is useful and fun at one table is not going to universally be useful and fun at all tables.<br /> <br /> Sounds like it was a fun encounter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387965#post1387965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the productivity? Why aren't use asking DrLoveMonkey the same question? Or is that a question that only matters if someone holds a different position than your own?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only reasons I use this forum is to get ideas to help me enjoy Exalted and to help other people enjoy Exalted more.<br /> <br /> If someone says &quot;this isn't fun for me&quot;, I'll happy spend twelve pages helping them have fun. I have no intention of spending so much as a single page arguing with someone about how to play the game right.<br /> <br /> I didn't/don't understand your posts and didn't see a productive conversation happening, so I stopped responding until DrLoveMonkey and yourself came to a place where I felt I could help. I understand why DrLoveMonkey is posting: if I understood why you were posting I'd try to help you, I don't understand so I asked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387965#post1387965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To actually discuss the topic of the thread. I have my opinions about it, you have your opinions about it, they differ... so I'd like to see if there's a reason beyond play style to actually consider here.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game is the game.<br /> <br /> You can make a compelling argument that the game is wrong... but that doesn't change the words printed in the rulebook.<br /> <br /> You are right that I like to reduce complex issues down to a binary. It's how my brain works. You are welcome to voice your opinion. My opinion isn't any more valid or correct than your opinion.<br /> <br /> My entire point is that I do what DrLoveMonkey is suggesting, and I love the Hardness mechanic.<br /> <br /> You don't love it, and that is fine. Your opinion is valid. If you are happy not loving it, then carry on with my blessing. When I present a binary option like &quot;change the rules or change your playstyle&quot; then I'm posting from the assumption that, like me, you are using the Exalted community because you want to enhance your game. If that's not why you're posting, then I can see why my posts aren't helpful to you: I'm treating this as a problem to be fixed. It is not my intent to invalidate your feelings, and I apologise if that's what I've been doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387965#post1387965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like trying to debate against a Rule Zero Fallacy with someone that refuses to acknowledge that's what they're doing. You come off as so far into &quot;here's how we make low Hardness matter more,&quot; mindset that you don't realize that you're also coming off as arguing that low Hardness needs to be lifted up; whether by changes to style, rules or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted 3E does not work like other RPGs, including Exalted 2E and 1E.<br /> <br /> If you approach 3E like a &quot;typical&quot; RPG, then many of the rules and setting elements will not be fun.<br /> <br /> I've found (false binary) that you can either assume the game is wrong (and either try to fix it, or do as you have done and soldier on against game elements that are not fun) or you can assume you are playing wrong (and play differently).<br /> <br /> Some 3E mechanics are wrong. I haven't found any playstyle that makes the Naval Combat system fun.<br /> <br /> But mostly, the system just isn't intuitive. If you change the way you play to reflect the way the game is nudging you, rather than the way you think you should play, then suddenly it becomes fun. This isn't limited to Hardness. <br /> <br /> If you are having fun, then play however you like. This isn't <i>actually</i> a right/wrong dichotomy -- it's really about subjective levels of fun. If you are having fun, you are doing it right.<br /> <br /> But my point isn't &quot;if you change the way you play, Hardness is more useful&quot;. My point is &quot;if you play in line with how the game is built, then you'll have more fun&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387965#post1387965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you realize that this sort of questioning of my motives negatively impacts the way more innocent intended questions are intended to be taken?</div> </div> </div> </div>I... continue to not understand what you are saying.<br /> <br /> I want to know what your motives are so we can have a productive discussion. I cannot infer motive from what you have written, and I would be grateful if you could clarify. If you'd rather not engage with the questions I'm asking, I have no power to compel you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387965#post1387965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK. We both agree that low Hardness is, by itself, a niche effect that's generally only taken as part of a pack of effects; and thus the answer to the general question of the thread is, &quot;not very, but you'll probably have it from one of those packages, and when it is useful hey, you'll have it.&quot;<br /> <br /> We don't need to debate about how good DoOM is, or if Solar sorcerers perhaps get a bit too much for the investment, or any of that? Most of the last 4 pages really?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also &quot;high&quot; Hardness. Hardness is a niche effect. Like Resolve. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386571-how-useful-is-hardness-at-low-values?p=1387965#post1387965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hardness, as a supernatural/superhuman effect, has a cost to it. All the cool packages that include it seem safe to assume would be cheaper if they didn't include Hardness.<br /> <br /> As a hypothetical thought experiment, imagine players could pick between two different versions of DoOM. One RAW, and the other without the Hardness attached. As Charms the cost the buy them is inherently the same. So, the second version of DoOM, as it gives less, should still cost less, right? It would be fair to say, cost 1m less to activate? <br /> <br /> Because that's part of the issue beyond agreeing that low Hardness is already a relatively niche effect that most people only have because it's part of a bigger package. I can't buy my hypothetical no-Hardness DoOM where I can get the part I'd use a lot, without the part I barely if ever use, and save 1m per use. I've got to take the package deal.<br /> <br /> So I feel like I should be getting something for what I'm paying for. Isn't that a fair feeling to have about this?</div> </div> </div> </div>All feelings are fair feelings. Your feelings are valid. You have every right to not like Hardness.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure your underpinning thoughts on &quot;costing&quot; Hardness are valid.<br /> <br /> You can't get Hardness in isolation, like you can't get &quot;Overwhelming&quot; on a weapon without also getting &quot;Damage&quot;. Costing the value of &quot;Overwhelming&quot; seperate from &quot;Damage&quot; is a pretty difficult task -- even though there are many effects that give increased Overwhelming from Charms to Tags to weapon class, which may or may not be linked to increased Damage (or decreased Accuracy/Defence). Likewise costing Hardness seperate from the other effects it is packaged with is... really difficult.<br /> <br /> I think DoOM without Hardness is probably still worth 3m. I also think that a standalone Charm that just gave Hardness 4 for a tick is <i>probably</i> also worth 3m (maybe 2m, depending on how it interacts with things like Diamond Body Prana).<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Low Hardness (1-7) is useful because it stops Anima Flux and low Initative damaging Decisive attacks. That's what it's for. That's why it's useful.<br /> <br /> High Hardness (8+) shares all the advantages of low Hardness and also forces your opponent to build more Initative before attacking you with a straight attack. It is often found on Heavy Armor, and combines with high Soak -- this combination helps you tank combats.<br /> <br /> Low Hardness remains useful, because it is usually tied to convenient, low cost, effects where High Hardness is usually tied to inconvenient, high cost, effects. Low Hardness covers weaknesses in the High Hardness powersets, and tend to be part of packages which have useful effects outside of Hardness.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Needless to say, I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar32_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"32\" data-vbnamecard=\"32\">Synapse</a> and am grateful for the helpful example provided. Very illustrative, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-14-2020, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}